1
00:01:54,113 --> 00:01:57,850
Lord Henry Wotton had set himself early in life to the serious study ...

2
00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:02,396
of the great aristocratic art of doing absolutely nothing .

3
00:02:02,496 --> 00:02:04,231
He lived only for pleasure ...

4
00:02:04,331 --> 00:02:07,359
but his greatest pleasure was to observe the emotions of his friends ...

5
00:02:07,459 --> 00:02:10,779
while experiencing none of his own .

6
00:02:10,879 --> 00:02:16,667
He diverted himself by exercising a subtle influence on the lives of others .

7
00:02:19,346 --> 00:02:21,923
Eighteen , I think you said , sir .

8
00:02:24,351 --> 00:02:27,011
- Shall I wait , sir ? - Yes .

9
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:34,220
Among Lord Henry 's friends was the painter Basil Hallward .

10
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,306
He had been strangely secretive about his latest painting ...

11
00:02:37,406 --> 00:02:39,433
and Lord Henry , sensing a mystery ...

12
00:02:39,533 --> 00:02:43,986
determined to discover what it was that his friend wished to conceal .

13
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:48,491
I 'm sorry , my lord , Mr. Hallward is not at home .

14
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:52,537
Mr. Hallward doesn 't wish to be disturbed .

15
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:18,472
It 's your best work , Basil . The best thing you 've ever done .

16
00:03:18,572 --> 00:03:21,809
Of course , I can 't believe that anyone is really as handsome as that portrait .

17
00:03:21,909 --> 00:03:24,687
Who is he ? What 's his name ? Why are you being so secretive about it ?

18
00:03:24,787 --> 00:03:25,896
It 's a great painting .

19
00:03:25,996 --> 00:03:28,607
You ought to send it to the Grosvenor and let everyone admire it .

20
00:03:28,707 --> 00:03:31,443
- I shall not send it anywhere . - But why ?

21
00:03:31,543 --> 00:03:33,754
I 've put too much of myself into it .

22
00:03:34,254 --> 00:03:37,658
I knew you 'd laugh , but it 's true all the same .

23
00:03:37,758 --> 00:03:41,495
Well , there certainly isn 't any resemblance between you and this young Adonis .

24
00:03:41,595 --> 00:03:45,666
You have an intellectual expression , and intellect destroys the beauty of any face .

25
00:03:45,766 --> 00:03:48,544
Don 't flatter yourself , Basil . You 're not in the least like him .

26
00:03:48,644 --> 00:03:52,172
Of course I 'm not like him . And I 'm glad of it .

27
00:03:52,272 --> 00:03:54,967
" The Wisdom of Buddha . "

28
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:57,469
You always did have a passion for virtue , Basil .

29
00:03:57,569 --> 00:03:59,221
Why are you glad you 're not like him ?

30
00:03:59,321 --> 00:04:01,515
We suffer for what the gods give us ...

31
00:04:01,615 --> 00:04:04,393
and I 'm afraid Dorian Gray will pay for his good looks .

32
00:04:04,493 --> 00:04:07,354
Dorian Gray . Is that his name ?

33
00:04:07,454 --> 00:04:10,573
Yes . I didn 't intend to tell it to you .

34
00:04:12,918 --> 00:04:15,946
If I 'm going to keep visiting you , I 'll have to send some good sherry .

35
00:04:16,046 --> 00:04:19,283
- Why didn 't you intend to tell me his name ? - I can 't explain .

36
00:04:19,383 --> 00:04:22,244
As I 've grown older , I 've come to love secrecy .

37
00:04:22,344 --> 00:04:24,204
I suppose that sounds foolish to you .

38
00:04:24,304 --> 00:04:27,958
Come into the garden . It doesn 't sound foolish to me at all .

39
00:04:28,058 --> 00:04:30,878
You forget that I am married and that the one charm of marriage ...

40
00:04:30,978 --> 00:04:34,506
is that it makes a life of deception absolutely necessary to both parties .

41
00:04:34,606 --> 00:04:37,134
I believe you are really a very good husband , Harry ...

42
00:04:37,234 --> 00:04:40,012
but that you are thoroughly ashamed of your own virtues .

43
00:04:40,112 --> 00:04:42,931
- Your cynicism is simply a pose . - Being natural is simply a pose ...

44
00:04:43,031 --> 00:04:46,143
and the most irritating pose I know . But you haven 't answered my question .

45
00:04:46,243 --> 00:04:49,647
I want to know the real reason why you won 't exhibit Dorian Gray 's picture .

46
00:04:49,747 --> 00:04:53,901
There is really very little to tell , Harry . Besides , I 'm afraid you will hardly believe it .

47
00:04:54,001 --> 00:04:56,570
I can believe anything provided that it is quite incredible .

48
00:04:56,670 --> 00:04:58,781
I 'm afraid this will seem so .

49
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:03,077
There is something I can 't quite understand .

50
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:06,205
- Something mystic about it . - Mystic ?

51
00:05:06,305 --> 00:05:10,084
I don 't know how to explain it , but whenever Dorian poses for me ...

52
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:14,004
it seems as if a power outside myself were guiding my hand .

53
00:05:14,104 --> 00:05:18,884
It 's as if the painting had a life of its own , independent of me .

54
00:05:18,984 --> 00:05:21,136
That 's why I 'm not going to exhibit it .

55
00:05:21,236 --> 00:05:23,764
It belongs rightfully to Dorian , and I shall give it to him .

56
00:05:23,864 --> 00:05:27,393
I want to meet this extraordinary young man . I think we shall be friends .

57
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:30,813
I choose my friends for their good looks and my enemies for their good intellects .

58
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:33,440
A man cannot be too careful in his choice of enemies .

59
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:36,985
Harry , I despise your principles , but I do enjoy the way you express them .

60
00:05:37,085 --> 00:05:38,779
I like persons better than principles ...

61
00:05:38,879 --> 00:05:41,615
and persons with no principles better than anything else .

62
00:05:41,715 --> 00:05:44,284
- Now I remember . - Remember what , Harry ?

63
00:05:44,384 --> 00:05:49,123
- Where I heard the name of Dorian Gray . - Where was it ?

64
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:52,084
Well , don 't look so startled . It was at my Aunt Agatha 's .

65
00:05:52,184 --> 00:05:54,795
My aunt told me that she had discovered a wonderful young man ...

66
00:05:54,895 --> 00:05:58,006
who was going to help with her charities and that his name was Dorian Gray .

67
00:05:58,106 --> 00:06:01,510
I pictured somebody with spectacles and lank hair ...

68
00:06:01,610 --> 00:06:04,096
tramping about on huge feet , and so I avoided meeting him .

69
00:06:04,196 --> 00:06:05,931
That 's a very common type of butterfly .

70
00:06:06,031 --> 00:06:09,143
Limenitis sibylla . It hardly belongs in a gentleman 's garden .

71
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:12,187
- I 'm glad you didn 't meet Dorian Gray . - Why ?

72
00:06:12,287 --> 00:06:14,314
I don 't want you to meet him .

73
00:06:18,043 --> 00:06:20,202
Who 's that at your piano , Basil ?

74
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:37,671
- You 've come early today , Dorian . - Have I ?

75
00:06:37,771 --> 00:06:40,174
You must lend me these pieces , Basil . I want to learn them .

76
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:42,176
Depends on how you sit this afternoon .

77
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:44,261
I thought the picture was going to be done today .

78
00:06:44,361 --> 00:06:45,679
It will be .

79
00:06:45,779 --> 00:06:48,223
Please go on , Mr. Gray . You play brilliantly .

80
00:06:48,323 --> 00:06:51,059
This is Lord Henry Wotton , Dorian . An old Oxford friend of mine .

81
00:06:51,159 --> 00:06:52,853
My aunt has spoken to me about you .

82
00:06:52,953 --> 00:06:55,731
You are one of her favorites and one of her victims too .

83
00:06:55,831 --> 00:06:59,151
- You shouldn 't go in for philanthropy . - Harry , I want to finish this picture .

84
00:06:59,251 --> 00:07:01,320
Would you think it rude if I asked you to go away ?

85
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:02,613
Am I to go , Mr. Gray ?

86
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:05,866
- Stay and tell me why not philanthropy . - You don 't really mind , do you , Basil ?

87
00:07:05,966 --> 00:07:08,952
You 've told me that you liked your sitters to have someone to chat to .

88
00:07:09,052 --> 00:07:11,455
Sit down then , Harry .

89
00:07:11,555 --> 00:07:13,332
Now , Dorian , get up on the platform ...

90
00:07:13,432 --> 00:07:15,793
and don 't pay any attention to what Lord Henry says .

91
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:20,047
He has a bad influence over his friends , with the single exception of myself .

92
00:07:20,147 --> 00:07:22,299
Have you really a bad influence , Lord Henry ?

93
00:07:22,399 --> 00:07:25,219
There 's no such thing as a good influence , Mr. Gray .

94
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:28,096
- All influence is immoral . - Why ?

95
00:07:28,196 --> 00:07:30,599
Because the aim of life is self-development .

96
00:07:30,699 --> 00:07:33,477
To realize one 's nature perfectly .

97
00:07:33,577 --> 00:07:35,687
That 's what we 're here for .

98
00:07:35,787 --> 00:07:38,232
A man should live out his life fully and completely ...

99
00:07:38,332 --> 00:07:41,443
give form to every feeling , expression to every thought ...

100
00:07:41,543 --> 00:07:43,487
reality to every dream .

101
00:07:43,587 --> 00:07:47,658
Every impulse that we suppress broods in the mind and poisons us .

102
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:51,703
There 's only one way to get rid of a temptation and that 's to yield to it .

103
00:07:51,803 --> 00:07:54,456
Resist it and the soul grows sick ...

104
00:07:54,556 --> 00:07:57,835
with longing for the things it has forbidden to itself .

105
00:07:57,935 --> 00:08:01,713
There is nothing that can cure the soul but the senses .

106
00:08:01,813 --> 00:08:06,093
Just as there is nothing that can cure the senses but the soul .

107
00:08:06,193 --> 00:08:08,929
Turn your head a little more to the left , Dorian .

108
00:08:09,029 --> 00:08:11,098
The gods have been good to you , Mr. Gray .

109
00:08:11,198 --> 00:08:12,349
Why do you say that ?

110
00:08:12,449 --> 00:08:14,101
You have the most marvelous youth ...

111
00:08:14,201 --> 00:08:17,437
- ... and youth is the one thing worth having . - I don 't feel that , Lord Henry .

112
00:08:17,537 --> 00:08:20,065
You don 't feel it now , but some day you 'll feel it terribly .

113
00:08:20,165 --> 00:08:22,776
What the gods give , they quickly take away .

114
00:08:22,876 --> 00:08:24,945
Time is jealous of you , Mr. Gray .

115
00:08:25,045 --> 00:08:28,991
Don 't squander the gold of your days . Live . Let nothing be lost upon you .

116
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:30,784
Be afraid of nothing .

117
00:08:30,884 --> 00:08:33,537
There is such a little time that your youth will last ...

118
00:08:33,637 --> 00:08:35,414
and you can never get it back .

119
00:08:35,514 --> 00:08:37,291
As we grow older , our memories are haunted ...

120
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:41,837
by the exquisite temptations we hadn 't the courage to yield to .

121
00:08:41,937 --> 00:08:43,881
The world is yours for a season .

122
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:46,842
It would be tragic if you realized too late ...

123
00:08:46,942 --> 00:08:48,927
as so many others do ...

124
00:08:49,027 --> 00:08:54,148
that there is only one thing in the world worth having , and that is youth .

125
00:08:54,616 --> 00:08:59,021
Dorian Gray had never heard the praise of folly so eloquently expressed .

126
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:02,482
The creed of pleasure soared into a philosophy of life ...

127
00:09:02,582 --> 00:09:06,153
while Dorian stood as if he were under a spell .

128
00:09:06,253 --> 00:09:10,866
He felt afraid of Lord Henry 's ideas and ashamed of himself for being afraid .

129
00:09:10,966 --> 00:09:14,119
It was as if he were learning to know himself for the first time ...

130
00:09:14,219 --> 00:09:18,665
as if a stranger had revealed his own most secret thoughts to him .

131
00:09:18,765 --> 00:09:22,294
For the first time he became conscious of his youth ...

132
00:09:22,394 --> 00:09:26,722
and conscious of the fact that one day he would lose it .

133
00:09:27,399 --> 00:09:29,009
My visit hasn 't been wasted .

134
00:09:29,109 --> 00:09:31,678
I 've found a rare and beautiful butterfly , Euvanesse antiope .

135
00:09:31,778 --> 00:09:35,439
It 's very unusual in England . Don 't you think it 's beautiful , Mr. Gray ?

136
00:09:35,824 --> 00:09:39,144
- Yes , Lord Henry , very beautiful . - You may sit down now , Dorian .

137
00:09:39,244 --> 00:09:40,771
I 'm glad you met Lord Henry .

138
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:43,523
- Are you glad , Mr. Gray ? - I 'm glad now .

139
00:09:43,623 --> 00:09:46,568
- I wonder if I shall always be glad . - " Always " ?

140
00:09:46,668 --> 00:09:49,446
That 's a dreadful word . It makes me shudder to hear it .

141
00:09:49,546 --> 00:09:50,822
Women are so fond of using it .

142
00:09:50,922 --> 00:09:53,867
They spoil every romance by trying to make it last forever .

143
00:09:53,967 --> 00:09:56,703
The only difference between a caprice and a life-long passion is ...

144
00:09:56,803 --> 00:09:58,330
the caprice lasts a little longer .

145
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:00,798
But I believe our hostess has appeared .

146
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,048
You 're just in time , darling ...

147
00:10:08,148 --> 00:10:10,384
to witness my signature to Dorian 's painting .

148
00:10:10,484 --> 00:10:11,969
Could I sign it too ?

149
00:10:12,069 --> 00:10:15,013
Well , I think you 're entitled to . Since you haven 't missed a sitting .

150
00:10:15,113 --> 00:10:16,647
Here .

151
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,191
G for Gladys .

152
00:10:20,368 --> 00:10:23,146
Which do you prefer , Gladys , Dorian Gray or his picture ?

153
00:10:23,246 --> 00:10:25,232
I like Dorian best .

154
00:10:25,332 --> 00:10:28,110
Heh . You prefer him today , but when you are a young lady ...

155
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:31,363
and are turning all the heads in London , you may prefer the portrait .

156
00:10:31,463 --> 00:10:34,574
For it will look just as it does today , but we shall all be changed .

157
00:10:34,674 --> 00:10:38,460
And not for the better . Your uncle and I and even Dorian .

158
00:10:39,012 --> 00:10:40,414
Dorian won 't change .

159
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:43,417
Dorian will stay just as he is until I 'm grown .

160
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,801
Won 't you , Dorian ?

161
00:10:46,561 --> 00:10:48,213
Of course I shall , darling .

162
00:10:48,313 --> 00:10:52,725
You may say goodbye now , precious . Nanny 's waiting . Come along . Hurry .

163
00:10:53,985 --> 00:10:56,471
- On your way . - What about me , young lady ?

164
00:10:56,571 --> 00:10:58,932
Has Dorian Gray stolen you from me completely ?

165
00:10:59,032 --> 00:11:01,476
- Goodbye , Lord Henry . - Heh .

166
00:11:01,576 --> 00:11:04,862
When this is known , I shall be torn to shreds in every drawing room in London .

167
00:11:05,205 --> 00:11:07,607
Don 't you think a gentleman should remove his hat ...

168
00:11:07,707 --> 00:11:09,401
in the presence of a lady , Parker ?

169
00:11:11,503 --> 00:11:15,032
I never take off my hat except when I 'm out of doors .

170
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:18,167
She 'll be as lovely as your sister was , Basil .

171
00:11:18,635 --> 00:11:20,203
Yes .

172
00:11:20,303 --> 00:11:23,457
But I 'm afraid Dorian has stolen her heart from me too .

173
00:11:23,557 --> 00:11:28,886
I must congratulate you , Basil . Look at yourself , Mr. Gray .

174
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:54,661
As I grow old , this picture will remain always young .

175
00:11:58,425 --> 00:12:00,243
If it were only the other way .

176
00:12:00,343 --> 00:12:04,581
If it were I who was always to be young and the picture that was to grow old .

177
00:12:04,681 --> 00:12:06,833
You would hardly care for such an arrangement , Basil .

178
00:12:06,933 --> 00:12:09,669
- It would be hard lines on your work . - I should object strongly .

179
00:12:09,769 --> 00:12:13,006
You oughtn 't to express such a wish in the presence of that cat , Dorian .

180
00:12:13,106 --> 00:12:16,558
It 's one of the 73 great gods of Egypt and is quite capable of granting your wish .

181
00:12:18,278 --> 00:12:19,805
Lord Henry is right .

182
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:22,606
I know now that when one loses one 's youth , one loses everything .

183
00:12:23,533 --> 00:12:27,604
Perhaps a cup of tea will bring you around . You 'll have some , too , won 't you , Harry ?

184
00:12:27,704 --> 00:12:29,773
Or do you object to such simple pleasures ?

185
00:12:29,873 --> 00:12:33,242
I adore simple pleasures . They 're the last refuge of the complex .

186
00:12:34,085 --> 00:12:36,321
It 's more than a painting . It 's part of myself .

187
00:12:36,421 --> 00:12:39,783
As soon as you 're varnished and framed , Dorian , you will be sent home .

188
00:12:39,883 --> 00:12:41,701
You can do whatever you like with yourself .

189
00:12:41,801 --> 00:12:45,622
Better send along the Egyptian cat . The god and the picture shouldn 't be separated .

190
00:12:45,722 --> 00:12:48,090
I will , if Dorian wants it .

191
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:53,463
If only the picture could change , and I could be always what I am now .

192
00:12:53,563 --> 00:12:55,257
For that I would give everything .

193
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:58,468
Yes , there 's nothing in the whole world I would not give .

194
00:12:58,568 --> 00:13:00,769
I would give my soul for that .

195
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:16,194
Dorian began to venture alone on warm summer evenings ...

196
00:13:16,294 --> 00:13:19,329
into surroundings which were strange to him .

197
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:26,204
Filled with curiosity about places and people remote from his own experience ...

198
00:13:26,304 --> 00:13:29,249
he wandered to the half-world of London ...

199
00:13:29,349 --> 00:13:32,919
the words of Lord Henry vibrating in his mind .

200
00:13:33,019 --> 00:13:37,681
" Live . Let nothing be lost upon you . Be afraid of nothing . "

201
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:05,792
The Two Turtles is honored by the visit of a gentleman .

202
00:14:10,473 --> 00:14:12,424
If you please , sir .

203
00:14:52,265 --> 00:14:55,377
I give you the sweetheart of the Two Turtles .

204
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:58,338
Our own Sibyl Vane !

205
00:15:13,036 --> 00:15:18,984
Snow was very plentiful And crumbs were very few

206
00:15:19,084 --> 00:15:21,278
When a weather-beaten sparrow

207
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:25,615
Through a mansion window flew

208
00:15:25,715 --> 00:15:29,536
Her eye fell on a golden cage

209
00:15:29,636 --> 00:15:33,915
A sweet love song she heard

210
00:15:34,015 --> 00:15:37,544
Sung by a pet canary there

211
00:15:37,644 --> 00:15:42,090
A handsome yellow bird

212
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:47,345
He said to her , " Miss Sparrow I 've been struck by Cupid 's arrow

213
00:15:47,445 --> 00:15:52,482
Will you share my cage with me ? "

214
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:56,396
She looked up at his castle

215
00:15:56,496 --> 00:16:00,358
With its ribbon and its tassel

216
00:16:00,458 --> 00:16:06,997
And in plaintive tones said she

217
00:16:08,299 --> 00:16:12,078
" Goodbye , little yellow bird

218
00:16:12,178 --> 00:16:16,041
I 'd rather brave the cold

219
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:18,918
On a leafless tree

220
00:16:19,018 --> 00:16:22,797
Than a prisoner be

221
00:16:22,897 --> 00:16:27,886
In a cage of gold "

222
00:16:30,697 --> 00:16:33,767
I 'd gladly introduce you , sir , but she 's proud .

223
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:35,984
She won 't meet anybody .

224
00:16:39,831 --> 00:16:41,608
Come , my delightful dove .

225
00:16:41,708 --> 00:16:45,702
Descend and make a pilgrimage with me among these mortals .

226
00:16:51,468 --> 00:16:54,829
The spoiled and petted yellow bird

227
00:16:54,929 --> 00:16:57,957
Could scarce believe it true

228
00:16:58,057 --> 00:17:01,586
That a common sparrow should refuse

229
00:17:01,686 --> 00:17:05,799
A bird with blood so blue

230
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:11,805
He told her the advantages Of riches and of gold

231
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:15,266
She answered that her liberty

232
00:17:15,366 --> 00:17:19,562
For gold could not be sold

233
00:17:19,662 --> 00:17:24,109
She said , " I must be going " But he cried , " No , no , it 's snowing

234
00:17:24,209 --> 00:17:29,197
And the wintry winds so blow

235
00:17:29,297 --> 00:17:32,617
Stay with me , my little dearie

236
00:17:32,717 --> 00:17:36,788
For without you , it would be dreary "

237
00:17:36,888 --> 00:17:42,759
But she only sighed , " Ah , no "

238
00:17:44,187 --> 00:17:47,173
" Goodbye , little yellow bird

239
00:17:48,441 --> 00:17:52,846
I 'd gladly mate with you

240
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:57,183
I love you , little yellow bird

241
00:17:57,283 --> 00:18:01,813
But I love my freedom too

242
00:18:01,913 --> 00:18:06,276
So goodbye , little yellow bird

243
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:10,864
I 'd rather brave the cold

244
00:18:10,964 --> 00:18:14,033
On a leafless tree

245
00:18:14,133 --> 00:18:17,871
Than a prisoner be

246
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:21,040
In a cage

247
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:25,177
Of gold "

248
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:44,147
She 's taken with you , sir . Say the word and I 'll take you backstage .

249
00:18:44,247 --> 00:18:46,114
Thank you , no .

250
00:18:49,544 --> 00:18:54,115
Night after night Dorian went to the Two Turtles to watch Sibyl Vane .

251
00:18:54,215 --> 00:18:56,576
A patron of the arts , Mrs. Vane .

252
00:18:56,676 --> 00:18:59,496
He 's come to the Two Turtles each evening for a fortnight .

253
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:02,839
He wants to tell you how much he admires your daughter .

254
00:19:04,767 --> 00:19:07,587
If you will permit me , I have a request to make .

255
00:19:07,687 --> 00:19:09,464
You 're very kind , sir .

256
00:19:09,564 --> 00:19:13,760
Miss Vane , will you sing " The Little Yellow Bird " for me now ?

257
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:15,803
She will , sir , gladly .

258
00:19:15,903 --> 00:19:18,890
But there 's no one to play for me . Everyone 's gone .

259
00:19:18,990 --> 00:19:21,351
I think I might manage the accompaniment .

260
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,902
You will , won 't you , dearie ?

261
00:19:24,954 --> 00:19:26,530
Yes .

262
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:30,075
On one condition .

263
00:19:33,004 --> 00:19:34,496
Please .

264
00:19:39,886 --> 00:19:43,129
I apologize for my daughter .

265
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:57,512
So goodbye , little yellow bird

266
00:19:57,612 --> 00:20:02,350
I 'd rather brave the cold

267
00:20:02,450 --> 00:20:05,770
On a leafless tree

268
00:20:05,870 --> 00:20:09,732
Than a prisoner be

269
00:20:09,832 --> 00:20:16,079
In a cage of gold

270
00:21:50,349 --> 00:21:54,344
It 's wonderful . Did ... ? Did you write it ?

271
00:21:56,814 --> 00:21:59,926
Frederic Chopin wrote it for a woman he loved .

272
00:22:00,026 --> 00:22:03,388
Her name was George Sand . Someday I 'll tell you about them .

273
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:05,438
I should like that .

274
00:22:12,371 --> 00:22:14,155
What did the music mean to you ?

275
00:22:15,124 --> 00:22:19,028
I don 't know . It is full of emotion .

276
00:22:19,128 --> 00:22:20,988
But it 's not happy .

277
00:22:21,088 --> 00:22:23,491
No , it 's not happy .

278
00:22:23,591 --> 00:22:25,500
Why was he unhappy ?

279
00:22:31,933 --> 00:22:35,002
Perhaps because he felt his youth slipping away from him .

280
00:22:35,102 --> 00:22:37,839
- What an odd thing for you to say . - Why ?

281
00:22:37,939 --> 00:22:41,558
- You are so young . - Yes .

282
00:22:41,859 --> 00:22:43,476
And you also .

283
00:22:46,697 --> 00:22:49,934
What is the music called ? Has it a name ?

284
00:22:50,034 --> 00:22:54,571
A kind of name . It is called " Prelude . "

285
00:23:36,539 --> 00:23:39,525
- Is this the way you watch Sibyl , Mother ? - You don 't understand , James .

286
00:23:39,625 --> 00:23:41,402
I wish I wasn 't going to Australia .

287
00:23:41,502 --> 00:23:43,696
I 'd cancel it if my articles hadn 't been signed .

288
00:23:43,796 --> 00:23:47,074
I want Sibyl to make a brilliant marriage . Actresses marry into the upper classes .

289
00:23:47,174 --> 00:23:49,911
- I almost did myself . - Who is this young dandy ? What 's his name ?

290
00:23:50,011 --> 00:23:51,871
Oh , I don 't know his name , but he 's rich .

291
00:23:51,971 --> 00:23:54,040
What 's his name , Sibyl ? How often has he been here ?

292
00:23:54,140 --> 00:23:56,250
- What are his intentions ? - I don 't know .

293
00:23:56,350 --> 00:23:59,879
But I do know his name . It is Sir Tristan .

294
00:23:59,979 --> 00:24:02,215
You don 't know his name and yet you permitted him to ...

295
00:24:02,315 --> 00:24:05,510
Your brother 's right , Sibyl , you ought not to have permitted such familiarity .

296
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:08,304
He is good . I know it . There is no evil in him .

297
00:24:08,404 --> 00:24:10,264
- Did you see his face ? - No , but I wish I had .

298
00:24:10,364 --> 00:24:13,100
If he ever does you any wrong , I 'll track him down and kill him .

299
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:16,312
Jim ! You 're foolish , Jim . Utterly foolish .

300
00:24:16,412 --> 00:24:18,940
You talk like one of the melodramas Mother used to act in .

301
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:22,860
That was when acting was understood . I received a lot of attention in those days .

302
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:26,572
All I say is watch over Sibyl , Mother . Watch over her while I 'm gone .

303
00:24:26,672 --> 00:24:28,164
Jim .

304
00:24:37,516 --> 00:24:39,210
You 're going away tonight .

305
00:24:39,310 --> 00:24:42,797
The ship will take you far away over the dark waters .

306
00:24:42,897 --> 00:24:46,099
Don 't let me remember you angry and troubled .

307
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,485
That 's better .

308
00:24:58,746 --> 00:25:01,030
Can 't you read what people are in their faces ?

309
00:25:03,459 --> 00:25:06,279
You think I 'm silly when I call him Sir Tristan .

310
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:08,614
But to me he 's like one of King Arthur 's knights ...

311
00:25:08,714 --> 00:25:11,284
that we used to read about when we were children ...

312
00:25:11,384 --> 00:25:16,080
who took the vow of chivalry to battle against all evil-doers .

313
00:25:16,180 --> 00:25:19,208
To defend the right to protect all women .

314
00:25:19,308 --> 00:25:22,635
To be true in friendship and faithful in love .

315
00:25:24,897 --> 00:25:29,309
You can 't go wrong with this one , sir . I 've never heard a sweeter warbler .

316
00:25:42,790 --> 00:25:44,407
Little yellow bird .

317
00:25:47,586 --> 00:25:50,156
- Late as usual , Harry . - Please forgive me , Aunt Agatha .

318
00:25:50,256 --> 00:25:52,658
Punctuality is the thief of time , Harry says .

319
00:25:52,758 --> 00:25:55,543
Victoria , darling , how nice .

320
00:25:56,595 --> 00:25:58,331
I love coming to your house , Aunt Agatha .

321
00:25:58,431 --> 00:26:00,958
It 's one of the few places I 'm likely to meet my husband .

322
00:26:02,226 --> 00:26:03,669
Oh , I 'm always dropping it .

323
00:26:03,769 --> 00:26:06,297
Mr. Gray has something terribly important to tell you , Harry .

324
00:26:06,397 --> 00:26:07,882
We 're all dying to learn what it is .

325
00:26:07,982 --> 00:26:11,010
I imagine it can wait until luncheon is over .

326
00:26:11,110 --> 00:26:13,012
I 'm vexed with you , Harry .

327
00:26:13,112 --> 00:26:16,015
Why do you try to persuade Mr. Gray to give up the East End ?

328
00:26:16,115 --> 00:26:19,060
He 's a wonderful musician , and they love his playing .

329
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,520
The East End is a very important problem .

330
00:26:21,620 --> 00:26:26,525
Quite so . It 's the problem of slavery , and we try to solve it by amusing the slaves .

331
00:26:26,625 --> 00:26:28,861
I suspect we 're interested in the poor ...

332
00:26:28,961 --> 00:26:30,655
in order to amuse ourselves .

333
00:26:30,755 --> 00:26:33,866
Especially as we grow older and are unfit for other amusements .

334
00:26:33,966 --> 00:26:36,702
Lord Henry , I wish you would tell me how to become young again .

335
00:26:36,802 --> 00:26:39,705
Can you remember any great errors that you committed in your early days ?

336
00:26:39,805 --> 00:26:41,916
- A great many , I fear . - Then commit them over again .

337
00:26:42,016 --> 00:26:44,669
To regain one 's youth , one has merely to repeat one 's follies .

338
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:45,878
A delightful theory .

339
00:26:45,978 --> 00:26:48,631
- A dangerous theory . - One of the great secrets of life .

340
00:26:48,731 --> 00:26:50,841
Most people die of a creeping common sense ...

341
00:26:50,941 --> 00:26:54,261
and discover too late that the only things one never regrets are one 's mistakes .

342
00:26:54,361 --> 00:26:57,723
But surely if one lives for oneself , one pays a terrible price for doing so .

343
00:26:57,823 --> 00:26:59,725
Yes , we are overcharged for everything now .

344
00:26:59,825 --> 00:27:03,354
- One has to pay in other ways than money . - What sort of ways , Sir Thomas ?

345
00:27:03,454 --> 00:27:08,484
I should fancy in remorse , in suffering , in ... Well , in the consciousness of degradation .

346
00:27:08,584 --> 00:27:10,820
No civilized man ever regrets a pleasure ...

347
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:13,531
and no uncivilized man ever knows what a pleasure is .

348
00:27:13,631 --> 00:27:15,950
I know what pleasure is . It 's to adore someone .

349
00:27:16,050 --> 00:27:18,828
In that case , I think I can guess what it is you have to tell me .

350
00:27:21,430 --> 00:27:23,499
But adoring someone is better than being adored .

351
00:27:23,599 --> 00:27:25,710
Being adored is a nuisance . You will discover ...

352
00:27:25,810 --> 00:27:28,421
that women treat us just as humanity treats its gods .

353
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:31,340
They worship us and keep bothering us to do something for them .

354
00:27:31,440 --> 00:27:33,092
Harry , you 're incorrigible .

355
00:27:33,192 --> 00:27:35,970
You must admit that women give men the very gold of their lives .

356
00:27:36,070 --> 00:27:38,431
But they invariably want it back in such small change .

357
00:27:38,531 --> 00:27:40,474
Women , as a witty Frenchman put it ...

358
00:27:40,574 --> 00:27:44,103
inspire us with the desire to do masterpieces and prevent us from carrying them out .

359
00:27:44,203 --> 00:27:45,271
I don 't understand you .

360
00:27:45,371 --> 00:27:47,815
You seem to know us women awfully well , Lord Henry .

361
00:27:47,915 --> 00:27:49,734
I am analyzing women at present .

362
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:52,319
The subject is less difficult than I was led to believe .

363
00:27:52,419 --> 00:27:54,947
Women represent the triumph of matter over mind ...

364
00:27:55,047 --> 00:27:58,868
just as men represent the triumph of mind over morals .

365
00:27:58,968 --> 00:28:01,454
These views are horrifying , Lady Agatha .

366
00:28:01,554 --> 00:28:04,248
I did not expect to hear the devil 's advocate at your table .

367
00:28:04,348 --> 00:28:06,834
I apologize for the intelligence of my remarks , Sir Thomas .

368
00:28:06,934 --> 00:28:10,136
I 'd forgotten that you were a member of parliament .

369
00:28:12,148 --> 00:28:15,301
You will forgive me , Lady Agatha , if I leave at once .

370
00:28:15,401 --> 00:28:18,095
Before the quail , Sir Thomas ? The first quail of the season ?

371
00:28:18,195 --> 00:28:19,805
I ordered them especially for you .

372
00:28:19,905 --> 00:28:22,183
No , surely not before the quail , Sir Thomas .

373
00:28:22,283 --> 00:28:25,436
Think with the Liberals and eat with the Tories . Isn 't that the rule ?

374
00:28:25,536 --> 00:28:28,647
How men argue . I can never make out what they 're talking about .

375
00:28:28,747 --> 00:28:30,399
Do sit down , Sir Thomas .

376
00:28:30,499 --> 00:28:33,360
Lord Henry 's ideas are demoralizing and delightful .

377
00:28:33,460 --> 00:28:36,162
They 're not to be taken seriously .

378
00:28:49,310 --> 00:28:53,255
I confess , I never could resist Lady Agatha 's quail .

379
00:28:55,107 --> 00:28:57,802
Well , Dorian , what have you to tell me that is so important ?

380
00:28:57,902 --> 00:29:00,930
From what you said at luncheon , my guess is that you 've fallen in love .

381
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:03,272
I 'm engaged to be married .

382
00:29:11,248 --> 00:29:13,943
Now that we 're on our way , perhaps you 'll tell me where we 're going .

383
00:29:14,043 --> 00:29:16,695
- Grosvenor Square , Number Seven . - It 's Dorian we 're going to see ?

384
00:29:16,795 --> 00:29:20,116
We 're going to pick him up and then see the young woman he 's engaged to marry .

385
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:23,911
- Dorian engaged ? To whom , Harry ? - To an actress in a cheap vaudeville .

386
00:29:24,011 --> 00:29:26,288
An actress . With dyed hair and a painted face ?

387
00:29:26,388 --> 00:29:28,165
Don 't run down dyed hair and painted faces .

388
00:29:28,265 --> 00:29:31,794
- There 's an extraordinary charm in them . - But surely you can 't be serious .

389
00:29:31,894 --> 00:29:35,297
- I hope I shall never be more serious . - You don 't approve .

390
00:29:35,397 --> 00:29:39,009
- You can 't possibly . - I never approve or disapprove of anything .

391
00:29:39,109 --> 00:29:42,263
Dorian falls in love with a beautiful girl and proposes to marry her . Why not ?

392
00:29:42,363 --> 00:29:43,722
Every experience is of value .

393
00:29:43,822 --> 00:29:46,642
Whatever can be said against marriage , it 's certainly an experience .

394
00:29:46,742 --> 00:29:48,310
Dorian will make this girl his wife .

395
00:29:48,410 --> 00:29:50,896
Six months later , he 'll become infatuated with someone else .

396
00:29:50,996 --> 00:29:54,525
- You think he could be so unfaithful ? - Faithfulness is merely laziness .

397
00:29:54,625 --> 00:29:57,403
Number Seven , sir .

398
00:29:58,671 --> 00:30:00,364
I 've been watching for you .

399
00:30:00,464 --> 00:30:02,241
Go to Lower Euston Road , Number 22 .

400
00:30:02,341 --> 00:30:03,701
Lower Euston Road , sir ?

401
00:30:03,801 --> 00:30:06,127
- Lower Euston Road . - Yes , sir .

402
00:30:08,555 --> 00:30:12,334
They 're always surprised when I give them that address . Hurry .

403
00:30:12,434 --> 00:30:14,920
I want you to get there in time to meet her before she sings .

404
00:30:15,020 --> 00:30:17,923
I hope you 'll always be as happy as you are at this moment , Dorian .

405
00:30:18,023 --> 00:30:20,593
Thank you , Basil . Our engagement is still a dead secret .

406
00:30:20,693 --> 00:30:23,470
- She 's not even told her mother . - What will your guardian say ?

407
00:30:23,570 --> 00:30:25,931
Lord Radley will be furious . But there 's nothing he can do .

408
00:30:26,031 --> 00:30:27,433
May I ask you a question ?

409
00:30:27,533 --> 00:30:29,768
At what particular point did you mention marriage ?

410
00:30:29,868 --> 00:30:31,604
I didn 't make any formal proposal , Harry .

411
00:30:31,704 --> 00:30:34,773
I told her I loved her , and she said she was not worthy to be my wife .

412
00:30:34,873 --> 00:30:37,735
- " Not worthy . " - Women are wonderfully practical .

413
00:30:37,835 --> 00:30:41,780
In situations of that kind , we often forget to say anything about marriage and they remind us .

414
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:43,949
Sibyl has made me forget your poisonous theories .

415
00:30:44,049 --> 00:30:46,452
- Which theories ? - Your theories about life , about pleasure .

416
00:30:46,552 --> 00:30:48,954
Pleasure is the only thing worth having a theory about .

417
00:30:49,054 --> 00:30:50,664
It 's nature 's sign of approval .

418
00:30:50,764 --> 00:30:54,251
When we 're happy , we 're always good . When we 're good , we 're not always happy .

419
00:30:54,351 --> 00:30:56,420
Sibyl is the answer to all your cynicism , Harry .

420
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:58,797
I believe you 'll understand that when you see her .

421
00:30:58,897 --> 00:31:03,177
So goodbye , little yellow bird

422
00:31:03,277 --> 00:31:07,932
I 'd rather brave the cold

423
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:10,935
On a leafless tree

424
00:31:11,035 --> 00:31:14,980
Than a prisoner be

425
00:31:15,080 --> 00:31:22,078
In a cage of gold

426
00:31:33,432 --> 00:31:35,918
This marriage is quite right . I didn 't think so at first ...

427
00:31:36,018 --> 00:31:38,003
but the moment we met her , I was convinced .

428
00:31:38,103 --> 00:31:40,381
She 's charming and innocent , transparently so .

429
00:31:40,481 --> 00:31:44,684
- I knew you would say that . - She 's all that you say , but I don 't agree .

430
00:31:46,528 --> 00:31:49,056
I believe she loves you so much , you have no need to marry her .

431
00:31:49,156 --> 00:31:51,433
What wickedness are you contemplating now ?

432
00:31:51,533 --> 00:31:53,978
I ought to be angry with you , Harry , but I 'm much too happy .

433
00:31:54,078 --> 00:31:56,105
All I know is that Sibyl is sacred to me .

434
00:31:56,205 --> 00:31:58,524
It 's only the sacred things that are worth touching .

435
00:31:58,624 --> 00:32:01,527
I begin to find you disgusting . Don 't listen to him , Dorian .

436
00:32:01,627 --> 00:32:04,530
Don 't worry , Basil . I 'm immune to his ideas now .

437
00:32:04,630 --> 00:32:07,783
In that case , I needn 't tell you how I should proceed if I were in your place .

438
00:32:07,883 --> 00:32:09,702
What would you do ? I 'm curious to know .

439
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:13,414
Well , I should invite her to come to my house to see Basil 's portrait .

440
00:32:13,514 --> 00:32:16,375
When she said it was time for her to go , I should ask her not to leave .

441
00:32:16,475 --> 00:32:19,211
She 'd be shocked , of course . I 'd pretend to be disappointed in her .

442
00:32:19,311 --> 00:32:21,714
If she still wished to go , I 'd become cold and indifferent .

443
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:24,049
I 'd , ask her to let herself out ...

444
00:32:24,149 --> 00:32:27,052
saying that I couldn 't bear sad farewells .

445
00:32:27,152 --> 00:32:30,139
But if she left , then I 'd believe her to be as good as she is beautiful ...

446
00:32:30,239 --> 00:32:32,599
and I 'd beg her forgiveness and marry her .

447
00:32:32,699 --> 00:32:34,852
I 've always thought your wickedness a pose .

448
00:32:34,952 --> 00:32:38,446
I know better now . You 're an unmitigated cad .

449
00:32:39,081 --> 00:32:41,741
Will you try my experiment , Dorian ?

450
00:32:45,504 --> 00:32:49,241
Miss Vane . Miss Vane , has Sir Tristan , as you have so charmingly called him ...

451
00:32:49,341 --> 00:32:53,078
ever invited you to see the wonderful portrait that Basil Hallward has made of him ?

452
00:32:53,178 --> 00:32:56,422
No , he hasn 't . I should love to see it . May I ?

453
00:32:56,932 --> 00:32:59,759
Of course you may , darling . Tonight , if you wish .

454
00:33:16,702 --> 00:33:21,405
I shall always remember this room , just as it is now .

455
00:33:22,082 --> 00:33:27,321
The lamplight , you at the piano , my own happiness .

456
00:33:44,104 --> 00:33:46,673
Your clock thinks it 's time for me to go home .

457
00:33:46,773 --> 00:33:48,634
Clocks can 't help being disagreeable .

458
00:33:48,734 --> 00:33:51,060
They think it 's their duty .

459
00:33:58,952 --> 00:34:00,646
It 's that cat .

460
00:34:00,746 --> 00:34:03,239
I thought I saw its eyes move .

461
00:34:03,540 --> 00:34:05,192
Perhaps you did .

462
00:34:05,292 --> 00:34:08,237
Lord Henry says it 's one of the 73 great gods of Egypt .

463
00:34:08,337 --> 00:34:12,957
- Doesn 't it frighten you ? - It does a little . Listen to this .

464
00:34:14,092 --> 00:34:18,831
Dawn follows Dawn , and Nights grow old And all the while this curious cat

465
00:34:18,931 --> 00:34:24,253
Lies couching on the Chinese mat With eyes of satin rimmed with gold .

466
00:34:24,353 --> 00:34:28,257
Get hence , you loathsome mystery ! Hideous animal , get hence !

467
00:34:28,357 --> 00:34:33,011
You wake in me each bestial sense You make me what I would not be .

468
00:34:33,111 --> 00:34:35,764
You make my creed a barren sham

469
00:34:35,864 --> 00:34:42,319
You wake foul dreams of sensual life

470
00:34:52,965 --> 00:34:56,118
What a strange poem . Who wrote it ?

471
00:34:56,218 --> 00:34:58,495
A brilliant young Irishman out of Oxford .

472
00:34:58,595 --> 00:35:01,005
His name is Oscar Wilde .

473
00:35:05,978 --> 00:35:08,387
Why do you look at me so strangely ?

474
00:35:09,189 --> 00:35:13,135
What would you do , Sibyl , if I should say to you ...

475
00:35:13,235 --> 00:35:16,562
" Don 't leave me now , don 't go home " ?

476
00:35:27,749 --> 00:35:29,450
What would you do , Sibyl ?

477
00:35:59,573 --> 00:36:02,775
I suppose I should have expected a conventional reaction .

478
00:36:04,911 --> 00:36:06,487
Good night , then .

479
00:36:08,248 --> 00:36:09,949
Good night .

480
00:36:10,667 --> 00:36:15,037
You don 't mind letting yourself out , do you ? I can 't bear sad farewells .

481
00:38:10,579 --> 00:38:13,565
A wise friend warned me that your innocence ...

482
00:38:13,665 --> 00:38:15,525
upon which I would have staked my life ...

483
00:38:15,625 --> 00:38:18,111
would fail to meet the test I set before you .

484
00:38:18,211 --> 00:38:21,823
I called his wisdom cynicism , but now I know better .

485
00:38:21,923 --> 00:38:23,408
You have killed my love .

486
00:38:23,508 --> 00:38:25,452
You have been false , not to me ...

487
00:38:25,552 --> 00:38:27,746
but to the ideal I had formed of you .

488
00:38:27,846 --> 00:38:31,541
You used to stir my imagination . Now you are nothing to me .

489
00:38:31,641 --> 00:38:34,836
I will never see you again . I will never mention your name .

490
00:38:34,936 --> 00:38:39,341
I will never think of you . Henceforth , I shall live only for pleasure .

491
00:38:39,441 --> 00:38:41,468
Everything else is meaningless .

492
00:38:41,568 --> 00:38:44,346
And if this leads me to the destruction of my soul ...

493
00:38:44,446 --> 00:38:47,015
then it is only you who are responsible .

494
00:38:47,115 --> 00:38:48,767
Do not try to see me .

495
00:38:48,867 --> 00:38:52,437
I shall leave England and not return for a long time .

496
00:38:52,537 --> 00:38:54,940
I am sending with this letter a gift of money ...

497
00:38:55,040 --> 00:38:58,235
which will compensate you for any disappointment you may feel .

498
00:38:58,335 --> 00:39:00,987
I have been living in a land of illusions .

499
00:39:01,087 --> 00:39:03,497
Now , I shall make an end of dreams .

500
00:39:04,090 --> 00:39:06,118
My real life begins .

501
00:39:06,218 --> 00:39:12,172
My own life , in which you cannot possibly have any part .

502
00:39:27,322 --> 00:39:29,565
Five minutes , Miss Vane .

503
00:39:44,798 --> 00:39:49,077
In spite of himself , Dorian was troubled by what he had done .

504
00:39:49,177 --> 00:39:52,539
His uneasy conscience made him avoid those he knew ...

505
00:39:52,639 --> 00:39:55,834
and all night he had wandered alone through the dimly lit streets ...

506
00:39:55,934 --> 00:39:59,344
and evil-looking houses of the London half-world .

507
00:40:00,146 --> 00:40:03,842
When at last he returned to his silent , shuttered house in Mayfair ...

508
00:40:03,942 --> 00:40:08,729
he could not overcome a sense of something ominous impending .

509
00:40:13,451 --> 00:40:17,654
His eye fell on the portrait Basil Hallward had painted of him .

510
00:40:38,810 --> 00:40:40,754
In the dim , shaded light ...

511
00:40:40,854 --> 00:40:45,217
the face appeared to him to be a little changed .

512
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:48,977
The expression looked somehow different .

513
00:40:49,696 --> 00:40:53,315
One would have said that there was a touch of cruelty in the mouth .

514
00:40:55,160 --> 00:40:57,236
It was very strange .

515
00:41:17,307 --> 00:41:21,135
There was no doubt that the whole expression had altered .

516
00:41:22,687 --> 00:41:26,974
The lines of cruelty about the mouth were unmistakable .

517
00:41:42,332 --> 00:41:45,409
There was no such expression on his face .

518
00:41:49,381 --> 00:41:53,535
If only the picture could change , and I could be always as I am now .

519
00:41:53,635 --> 00:41:55,704
For that I would give everything .

520
00:41:55,804 --> 00:41:59,207
Yes , there is nothing in the whole world I would not give .

521
00:41:59,307 --> 00:42:01,842
I would give my soul for that .

522
00:42:03,812 --> 00:42:07,097
But , surely , his wish had not been fulfilled .

523
00:42:07,857 --> 00:42:12,603
Such things were impossible . It was monstrous even to think of it .

524
00:42:15,448 --> 00:42:18,977
What if someone else observed the horrible change , his valet , perhaps ?

525
00:42:19,077 --> 00:42:23,405
What if Basil Hallward came and asked to look at his own picture ?

526
00:42:31,631 --> 00:42:34,993
But he was being ridiculous . This was a mere hallucination .

527
00:42:35,093 --> 00:42:38,378
An illusion brought on by his troubled senses .

528
00:42:38,972 --> 00:42:42,792
The picture had not changed . He was mad to think so .

529
00:42:42,892 --> 00:42:45,928
A painted canvas could not alter .

530
00:42:47,731 --> 00:42:51,176
He would look at it again after he had slept , when he was calmer ...

531
00:42:51,276 --> 00:42:54,603
and he would laugh at this fantastic idea .

532
00:42:56,573 --> 00:43:00,518
But in the afternoon when he returned to examine the portrait again ...

533
00:43:00,618 --> 00:43:02,687
fantastic as the idea was ...

534
00:43:02,787 --> 00:43:07,241
his memory of that cruel look was disturbingly vivid .

535
00:43:18,011 --> 00:43:22,422
It was true . The expression had altered .

536
00:43:23,224 --> 00:43:28,011
There was no doubt of it . It was incredible , and yet it was a fact .

537
00:43:29,731 --> 00:43:34,135
Was this portrait to become for him the emblem of his own conscience ?

538
00:43:34,235 --> 00:43:37,479
Would it teach him to loathe his own soul ?

539
00:43:39,240 --> 00:43:42,227
But if this painting was to be his conscience made visible ...

540
00:43:42,327 --> 00:43:44,479
then he would let it instruct him .

541
00:43:44,579 --> 00:43:46,606
He would give it no reason to reproach him .

542
00:43:46,706 --> 00:43:49,324
He would live purely and nobly .

543
00:43:52,420 --> 00:43:55,615
He had been cruel to Sibyl Vane . But it was not too late to make that right .

544
00:43:55,715 --> 00:43:57,826
She could still be his wife .

545
00:43:57,926 --> 00:44:00,286
He would marry her . They could be happy together .

546
00:44:00,386 --> 00:44:03,498
He implored her forgiveness . He blamed himself .

547
00:44:03,598 --> 00:44:06,508
He gave way to the luxury of self-reproach .

548
00:44:07,977 --> 00:44:11,513
When he finished the letter , he felt that he had been forgiven .

549
00:44:14,484 --> 00:44:17,394
Dorian , let me in . I must see you .

550
00:44:20,615 --> 00:44:23,525
Open the door , Dorian . I 'll not go away until I see you .

551
00:44:31,668 --> 00:44:34,202
Dorian , let me in .

552
00:44:38,716 --> 00:44:42,954
You shouldn 't lock yourself in like this , Dorian . I 'm sorry for it all , dreadfully sorry .

553
00:44:43,054 --> 00:44:45,623
- You mean about Sibyl Vane ? - Yes , of course .

554
00:44:45,723 --> 00:44:47,709
It 's all right now . I 'm actually grateful to you .

555
00:44:47,809 --> 00:44:49,377
I 've learned to know myself better .

556
00:44:49,477 --> 00:44:52,964
I know you will sneer at me , but from now on , I 'm going to do as my conscience bids me .

557
00:44:53,064 --> 00:44:56,551
- What on earth are you talking about ? - About Sibyl Vane . I 'm going to marry her .

558
00:44:56,651 --> 00:44:59,220
- Marry her ? - I know what you 're going to say .

559
00:44:59,320 --> 00:45:01,765
Something cynical about marriage . Don 't say it .

560
00:45:01,865 --> 00:45:05,810
Two weeks ago , I asked Sibyl to marry me . I 'm not going to break my word to her .

561
00:45:05,910 --> 00:45:08,104
- Then you don 't know . - Know what ?

562
00:45:08,204 --> 00:45:11,531
- Haven 't you read the morning papers ? - No , I haven 't .

563
00:45:18,423 --> 00:45:20,874
What is it , Harry ? What 's happened ?

564
00:45:27,265 --> 00:45:29,299
Sibyl Vane is dead .

565
00:45:49,245 --> 00:45:52,190
That 's why I hurried here . I didn 't want you to see anyone until I came .

566
00:45:52,290 --> 00:45:54,984
When I found you 'd locked yourself in , I assumed you knew about it .

567
00:45:55,084 --> 00:45:57,195
There 'll be an inquest . You mustn 't get involved .

568
00:45:57,295 --> 00:46:00,198
They don 't know your name at the theater , I suppose , so it 's all right .

569
00:46:00,298 --> 00:46:02,707
Did Sibyl ?

570
00:46:03,134 --> 00:46:06,121
- Tell me everything , Harry . - It was obviously not an accident .

571
00:46:06,221 --> 00:46:08,456
Though I suppose it must be put that way to the public .

572
00:46:08,556 --> 00:46:11,292
Half past 12 or so , she was leaving the theater with her mother ...

573
00:46:11,392 --> 00:46:14,546
when she said she 'd forgotten something and went back to her dressing room .

574
00:46:14,646 --> 00:46:17,048
She didn 't come down again . They found her on the floor .

575
00:46:17,148 --> 00:46:19,467
She 'd swallowed something . By mistake , they say .

576
00:46:19,567 --> 00:46:21,810
She died instantaneously .

577
00:46:23,029 --> 00:46:25,682
It 's tragic , but you mustn 't let yourself brood over it .

578
00:46:25,782 --> 00:46:28,852
You must learn to see it in its proper perspective .

579
00:46:28,952 --> 00:46:31,396
You must put it out of your mind . Come and dine with me .

580
00:46:31,496 --> 00:46:33,731
Afterwards , we 'll look in at the opera . Don Giovanni .

581
00:46:33,831 --> 00:46:36,283
Everybody 'll be there , and you can come to my sister 's box .

582
00:46:36,834 --> 00:46:39,112
So I have murdered Sibyl Vane ...

583
00:46:39,212 --> 00:46:43,366
- ... as surely as if I 'd cut her throat . - I can 't see why you should blame yourself .

584
00:46:43,466 --> 00:46:45,827
I suppose she foolishly thought she 'd lost you .

585
00:46:45,927 --> 00:46:47,954
But no woman destroys herself who isn 't already unbalanced ...

586
00:46:48,054 --> 00:46:49,330
Where do you keep your sherry ?

587
00:46:49,430 --> 00:46:51,040
If you 'd married this girl , you would 've been wretched ,

588
00:46:51,140 --> 00:46:52,709
and so in time would she have been .

589
00:46:52,809 --> 00:46:55,086
I assure you , the whole thing would have been an absolute failure .

590
00:46:55,186 --> 00:46:57,797
I remember your saying there 's a fatality about good resolutions .

591
00:46:57,897 --> 00:46:59,299
They 're always made too late .

592
00:46:59,399 --> 00:47:01,759
- Mine certainly were . - You should look upon this tragedy ...

593
00:47:01,859 --> 00:47:04,095
as an episode in the wonderful spectacle of life .

594
00:47:04,195 --> 00:47:07,974
What is it that has really happened ? Someone has killed herself for love of you .

595
00:47:08,074 --> 00:47:10,351
I wish that I 'd had such an experience .

596
00:47:10,451 --> 00:47:12,729
The women who have admired me ... There have been some .

597
00:47:12,829 --> 00:47:15,732
- have insisted on living on long after I have ceased to care for them ...

598
00:47:15,832 --> 00:47:18,735
or they to care for me . They 've become stout and tedious .

599
00:47:18,835 --> 00:47:20,778
When I meet them , they go in for reminiscences .

600
00:47:20,878 --> 00:47:23,406
That awful memory of woman . Drink , it 'll make you feel better .

601
00:47:23,506 --> 00:47:25,950
I found myself sitting next to such a woman the other night .

602
00:47:26,050 --> 00:47:28,286
She once proposed to sacrifice the whole world for me .

603
00:47:28,386 --> 00:47:31,164
Always a dreadful moment . It fills one with the terror of eternity .

604
00:47:31,264 --> 00:47:34,375
It happened years ago , but she dragged the whole thing out again ...

605
00:47:34,475 --> 00:47:38,296
and she assured me that I 'd spoiled her life . However , she ate an enormous dinner .

606
00:47:38,396 --> 00:47:42,467
Not one of the women I 've known would have done for me what Sibyl Vane did for you .

607
00:47:42,567 --> 00:47:44,886
But you haven 't told me yet if you will dine with me .

608
00:47:44,986 --> 00:47:46,638
I don 't feel up to it , Harry .

609
00:47:46,738 --> 00:47:48,765
Then perhaps you 'll join me later at the opera .

610
00:47:48,865 --> 00:47:52,143
My sister 's box number is 27 . It 's on the Grand Tier .

611
00:47:52,243 --> 00:47:55,647
You 'll see her name on the door . I hope to see you before half past 9 .

612
00:47:55,747 --> 00:47:58,608
I don 't want you to miss de Reszke in the duet .

613
00:48:12,972 --> 00:48:16,626
I 'm sorry , Mr. Hallward . Mr. Gray isn 't in . He 's gone to the opera .

614
00:48:16,726 --> 00:48:20,095
- To the opera ? - Yes , sir . Is there any message , sir ?

615
00:48:21,689 --> 00:48:24,432
No . No , I 'll come by in the morning .

616
00:48:47,924 --> 00:48:49,200
But in the morning ...

617
00:48:49,300 --> 00:48:52,328
Dorian no longer wanted the consolation of his friend ...

618
00:48:52,428 --> 00:48:54,497
nor his reproaches .

619
00:48:54,597 --> 00:48:57,375
His pride and his sense of guilt prompted him ...

620
00:48:57,475 --> 00:48:59,843
to assume an air of indifference .

621
00:49:05,817 --> 00:49:07,343
Hello , Basil . Sorry to keep you .

622
00:49:07,443 --> 00:49:09,721
- Have you had breakfast ? - Yes , I have , thank you .

623
00:49:09,821 --> 00:49:12,765
I 'm famished . You don 't mind if I have a bite while we talk ?

624
00:49:12,865 --> 00:49:14,649
Of course not .

625
00:49:16,994 --> 00:49:20,940
You went to the opera while Sibyl Vane was lying dead in some sordid lodging ?

626
00:49:21,040 --> 00:49:24,944
- What is past is past . - You call yesterday the past ?

627
00:49:25,044 --> 00:49:28,031
It 's only shallow people who require years to get rid of an emotion .

628
00:49:28,131 --> 00:49:29,574
A man who is master of himself ...

629
00:49:29,674 --> 00:49:32,410
can end a sorrow as easily as he can invent a pleasure .

630
00:49:32,510 --> 00:49:34,454
I don 't want to be at the mercy of my emotions .

631
00:49:34,554 --> 00:49:36,581
I want to use them , enjoy them , and dominate them .

632
00:49:36,681 --> 00:49:39,758
Something has changed you completely , Dorian .

633
00:49:40,643 --> 00:49:42,712
You look exactly the same .

634
00:49:42,812 --> 00:49:45,548
You talk as if you had no heart , no pity in you .

635
00:49:45,648 --> 00:49:47,050
You 've come too late .

636
00:49:47,150 --> 00:49:49,719
If you had come in yesterday at a particular moment ...

637
00:49:49,819 --> 00:49:52,513
about half past 5 or a quarter to 6 ...

638
00:49:52,613 --> 00:49:55,016
you would 've seen how deeply I was affected .

639
00:49:55,116 --> 00:49:58,603
Even Harry , who brought me the news , had no idea what I was going through .

640
00:49:58,703 --> 00:50:02,322
I suffered immensely . Then it passed away .

641
00:50:02,748 --> 00:50:06,319
I cannot repeat an emotion . No one can .

642
00:50:06,419 --> 00:50:09,530
This isn 't you talking , Dorian . These are Harry 's ideas .

643
00:50:09,630 --> 00:50:11,115
It has nothing to do with Harry .

644
00:50:11,215 --> 00:50:14,035
I suppose Harry didn 't give you that yellow book I saw on your table .

645
00:50:14,135 --> 00:50:15,787
- What 's wrong with it ? - Everything .

646
00:50:15,887 --> 00:50:19,297
It 's vile , evil , corrupt , decadent . I detest it .

647
00:50:20,892 --> 00:50:22,801
What would you like me to read , Basil ?

648
00:50:26,814 --> 00:50:28,515
Since you asked me .

649
00:50:29,859 --> 00:50:32,345
- " The Light of Asia . " - I 'm never without it .

650
00:50:32,445 --> 00:50:36,474
- The story of Buddha , isn 't it ? - The story of Buddha , a good man .

651
00:50:36,574 --> 00:50:39,901
- Promise me you 'll read it , Dorian . - I promise .

652
00:50:43,664 --> 00:50:47,235
You 've done a sketch of Sibyl . It 's charming . May I have it ?

653
00:50:47,335 --> 00:50:50,745
Of course . I must go now , Dorian .

654
00:50:51,172 --> 00:50:54,450
I 'm relieved to find you in such good spirits , in spite of what has happened .

655
00:50:54,550 --> 00:50:57,585
Thank you , Basil . It 's good of you to be so concerned .

656
00:50:59,388 --> 00:51:02,757
Before I go , I 'd like to look at the painting I did of you .

657
00:51:04,060 --> 00:51:05,628
There 's a screen in front of it .

658
00:51:05,728 --> 00:51:07,839
I thought the room looked different when I came in .

659
00:51:07,939 --> 00:51:09,882
The light was too strong on the portrait .

660
00:51:09,982 --> 00:51:11,175
Surely not .

661
00:51:11,275 --> 00:51:13,476
It 's an admirable place for it .

662
00:51:17,573 --> 00:51:18,808
Wait .

663
00:51:18,908 --> 00:51:20,726
You must not look at it .

664
00:51:20,826 --> 00:51:23,521
Not look at my own work ? You 're not serious .

665
00:51:23,621 --> 00:51:26,232
- Why shouldn 't I look at it ? - I don 't offer any explanation ...

666
00:51:26,332 --> 00:51:29,318
and you 're not to ask for any , but if you try to look at that picture ...

667
00:51:29,418 --> 00:51:32,238
on my word of honor , I will never speak to you again .

668
00:51:32,338 --> 00:51:35,533
What on earth is the matter with you ? I 'm planning to exhibit it next month .

669
00:51:35,633 --> 00:51:37,994
- That 's why I wanted to look at it . - Exhibit it ?

670
00:51:38,094 --> 00:51:40,371
But you told me a month ago , you would never exhibit it .

671
00:51:40,471 --> 00:51:42,832
You told Harry the same thing .

672
00:51:42,932 --> 00:51:46,377
At that time the painting had a strange fascination for me .

673
00:51:46,477 --> 00:51:49,338
It seemed almost to have a life of its own .

674
00:51:49,438 --> 00:51:53,349
It affected me so much , I felt I couldn 't let it be seen publicly .

675
00:51:54,610 --> 00:51:57,555
Perhaps you 've seen the same mysterious quality in it , Dorian ?

676
00:51:57,655 --> 00:52:00,057
Have you noticed something curious in the painting ?

677
00:52:00,157 --> 00:52:05,111
Something that at first did not strike you , but that revealed itself to you suddenly ?

678
00:52:05,955 --> 00:52:09,324
- I see you did . - I saw something in it .

679
00:52:09,792 --> 00:52:12,737
Something that seemed to be very curious .

680
00:52:12,837 --> 00:52:14,614
You were right .

681
00:52:14,714 --> 00:52:17,415
There can be something fatal about a portrait .

682
00:52:18,551 --> 00:52:20,912
I think I understand what you feel about it .

683
00:52:21,012 --> 00:52:22,914
And I respect your wishes .

684
00:52:23,014 --> 00:52:26,007
Perhaps someday you 'll recover from it , as I did .

685
00:52:26,434 --> 00:52:29,170
At any rate , I 'll certainly not let it destroy our friendship .

686
00:52:29,270 --> 00:52:30,922
I 'm glad of that .

687
00:52:31,022 --> 00:52:32,472
Goodbye , Dorian .

688
00:52:33,733 --> 00:52:35,350
Goodbye , Basil .

689
00:52:40,781 --> 00:52:44,143
It had been mad of him to allow the thing to remain , even for an hour ...

690
00:52:44,243 --> 00:52:47,480
in a room to which any of his friends had access .

691
00:52:47,580 --> 00:52:51,866
Henceforth , he must be on his guard against everyone .

692
00:53:01,927 --> 00:53:04,956
At the top of the house was his old schoolroom ...

693
00:53:05,056 --> 00:53:06,958
which had not been used for years .

694
00:53:07,058 --> 00:53:09,377
No one ever entered it .

695
00:53:09,477 --> 00:53:12,380
Nothing was in it but his old school books and his toys ...

696
00:53:12,480 --> 00:53:14,465
gathering dust and cobwebs .

697
00:53:14,565 --> 00:53:17,635
The picture could be safely hidden away there .

698
00:53:17,735 --> 00:53:21,521
He could lock it up . He himself would keep the key .

699
00:53:22,740 --> 00:53:26,067
There was no need for the servants ever to enter the room .

700
00:53:48,599 --> 00:53:53,087
He would have to let Victor go , and the others .

701
00:53:53,187 --> 00:53:56,723
He must bring new servants into the house .

702
00:54:07,368 --> 00:54:09,687
In this room , every moment of his childhood ...

703
00:54:09,787 --> 00:54:12,822
and its stainless purity came back to him .

704
00:54:13,916 --> 00:54:16,652
Here among the innocent souvenirs of his childhood ...

705
00:54:16,752 --> 00:54:20,705
the hideous portrait would be forever hidden away .

706
00:54:22,758 --> 00:54:27,038
The face painted in the canvas could grow bestial , sodden and unclean .

707
00:54:27,138 --> 00:54:32,383
No one would ever see it . No one , except himself .

708
00:54:35,146 --> 00:54:36,672
He was to have eternal youth ...

709
00:54:36,772 --> 00:54:40,266
while the portrait bore the burden of his shame .

710
00:54:44,155 --> 00:54:48,441
He was caught in an evil destiny .

711
00:54:52,163 --> 00:54:55,858
As the years passed , the miracle of Dorian 's changeless youth ...

712
00:54:55,958 --> 00:54:59,035
caused wonder but rarely suspicion .

713
00:54:59,420 --> 00:55:02,073
Even those who had heard the most evil things against him ...

714
00:55:02,173 --> 00:55:04,408
the strange rumors about his mode of life ...

715
00:55:04,508 --> 00:55:07,703
which spread through London and became the chatter of the clubs ...

716
00:55:07,803 --> 00:55:11,374
could not believe anything to his dishonor when they saw him .

717
00:55:11,474 --> 00:55:13,084
He had always the look of one ...

718
00:55:13,184 --> 00:55:16,587
who had kept himself unspotted from the world .

719
00:55:20,065 --> 00:55:25,012
But while he fascinated many , there were not a few who distrusted him .

720
00:55:25,112 --> 00:55:27,973
Curious stories were current about him .

721
00:55:28,073 --> 00:55:30,184
It was rumored that he had been seen in a low den ...

722
00:55:30,284 --> 00:55:32,478
in the distant parts of Whitechapel .

723
00:55:32,578 --> 00:55:35,564
His extraordinary absences became notorious ...

724
00:55:35,664 --> 00:55:38,776
and when he reappeared again in society , men would whisper to each other ...

725
00:55:38,876 --> 00:55:43,955
in corners , or pass him with a sneer , or look at him with cold , searching eyes .

726
00:55:44,465 --> 00:55:46,575
Some of those who had been most intimate with him ...

727
00:55:46,675 --> 00:55:49,794
appeared after a time to shun him .

728
00:55:50,387 --> 00:55:53,040
Women who , for his sake , had set convention at defiance ...

729
00:55:53,140 --> 00:55:56,676
were seen to grow pale if Dorian Gray entered the room .

730
00:55:57,603 --> 00:55:59,547
He could not endure to be long out of England ...

731
00:55:59,647 --> 00:56:03,718
or to be separated from the picture , it was such a part of his life .

732
00:56:03,818 --> 00:56:05,469
He was afraid that during his absence ...

733
00:56:05,569 --> 00:56:08,438
someone might gain access to the room where it was hidden .

734
00:56:09,824 --> 00:56:11,809
Then , suddenly , some night he would go down ...

735
00:56:11,909 --> 00:56:17,356
to dreadful places near Bluegate Fields , and stay there , day after day .

736
00:56:58,080 --> 00:57:01,525
When he had recovered from these visits to the abyss ...

737
00:57:01,625 --> 00:57:06,989
he would stand in front of the picture , sometimes loathing it and himself ...

738
00:57:07,089 --> 00:57:10,493
but filled at other times with that pride of individualism ...

739
00:57:10,593 --> 00:57:13,370
that is half the fascination of evil .

740
00:57:13,470 --> 00:57:16,165
He would examine with minute care the hideous lines ...

741
00:57:16,265 --> 00:57:18,459
that scarred the wrinkling forehead ...

742
00:57:18,559 --> 00:57:21,212
or crawled around the heavy sensual mouth ...

743
00:57:21,312 --> 00:57:26,974
wondering which were more horrible , the signs of sin or the signs of age .

744
00:57:28,485 --> 00:57:31,680
He found reasons to justify his actions .

745
00:57:31,780 --> 00:57:37,228
He told himself that man was a being with myriad lives and myriad sensations .

746
00:57:37,328 --> 00:57:41,190
To live a simple , sincere , honest life was hardly to live at all .

747
00:57:41,290 --> 00:57:46,195
Was insincerity such a terrible thing ? Dorian thought not .

748
00:57:46,295 --> 00:57:50,832
It was merely a method by which we could multiply our personalities .

749
00:57:51,842 --> 00:57:55,871
Yet , there was one person towards whom he found it difficult to be insincere .

750
00:57:55,971 --> 00:58:00,508
It was Basil Hallward 's niece , Gladys , who had loved him since she was a child .

751
00:58:01,477 --> 00:58:06,632
Goodbye , little yellow bird

752
00:58:06,732 --> 00:58:12,687
I 'd rather brave the cold

753
00:58:13,238 --> 00:58:16,433
On a leafless tree

754
00:58:16,533 --> 00:58:20,104
Than a prisoner be

755
00:58:20,204 --> 00:58:26,325
In a cage of gold

756
00:58:27,294 --> 00:58:31,156
I was close by and came in for a moment . I found this old song in your piano bench .

757
00:58:31,256 --> 00:58:32,950
It 's charming .

758
00:58:33,050 --> 00:58:35,578
So is the face that my uncle sketched on it .

759
00:58:35,678 --> 00:58:39,172
He did do it , didn 't he ? I know his style so well .

760
00:58:40,975 --> 00:58:43,377
Did she sing this song ?

761
00:58:43,477 --> 00:58:46,929
Who is she ? Do tell me about her .

762
00:58:47,773 --> 00:58:52,143
She died many years ago , when you were only a little girl .

763
00:58:54,238 --> 00:58:56,898
Did you love her very much , Dorian ?

764
00:58:58,200 --> 00:58:59,692
Yes .

765
00:59:05,082 --> 00:59:07,443
Goodbye , Dorian . I 'm looking forward to your party tonight .

766
00:59:07,543 --> 00:59:10,703
I 'm sure it will be wonderful . Your parties always are .

767
00:59:17,428 --> 00:59:19,788
I 'm not really as lovely as that picture , am I , darling ?

768
00:59:19,888 --> 00:59:21,332
Of course not .

769
00:59:22,766 --> 00:59:26,003
I think I 've discovered why Dorian hasn 't proposed to me .

770
00:59:26,103 --> 00:59:27,671
And I 've decided what to do about it .

771
00:59:27,771 --> 00:59:29,882
And what have you decided to do about it ?

772
00:59:29,982 --> 00:59:33,052
I 'm going to ask him to marry me , tonight , perhaps .

773
00:59:33,152 --> 00:59:34,845
What about David Stone ?

774
00:59:34,945 --> 00:59:36,764
You think he 'd take you to Dorian 's party ...

775
00:59:36,864 --> 00:59:39,141
- ... if he knew your intentions ? - Of course he would .

776
00:59:39,241 --> 00:59:42,311
Nothing petty about David , but I don 't intend to tell him .

777
00:59:42,411 --> 00:59:44,897
- No , don 't tell David . - David , you cad .

778
00:59:44,997 --> 00:59:46,982
I never thought you 'd be an eavesdropper .

779
00:59:47,082 --> 00:59:49,777
Don 't be alarmed about Dorian Gray . I 'm the one Gladys will marry .

780
00:59:49,877 --> 00:59:51,654
Of course , I have nothing to say about it .

781
00:59:51,754 --> 00:59:55,282
- I wouldn 't let you marry that devil . - I 'll not have you say anything against him .

782
00:59:55,382 --> 00:59:57,701
I don 't have to . There are plenty of others to say it .

783
00:59:57,801 --> 01:00:01,664
Lies and jealousy . There 's no evil in Dorian . Anybody can see that by looking at him .

784
01:00:01,764 --> 01:00:03,290
He hasn 't asked you yet .

785
01:00:03,390 --> 01:00:06,043
You heard what I said . I 'm going to ask him myself .

786
01:00:06,143 --> 01:00:10,714
- In front of all those people , I suppose . - I 'll get him alone . It 's a big house .

787
01:00:10,814 --> 01:00:13,641
- Good night , sir . - Good night , David .

788
01:01:01,657 --> 01:01:04,435
What 's wrong , Dorian ? Why don 't you answer me ?

789
01:01:04,535 --> 01:01:07,312
Is there something else ? Something I don 't know about ?

790
01:01:07,412 --> 01:01:09,398
You must have heard the stories they tell of me .

791
01:01:09,498 --> 01:01:11,984
- Don 't they frighten you ? - I don 't believe them .

792
01:01:12,084 --> 01:01:15,953
- Suppose I were to tell you that they 're true . - I will never believe anything evil of you .

793
01:01:19,383 --> 01:01:21,375
What do you know of evil ?

794
01:01:22,553 --> 01:01:25,046
I only know there is none in you .

795
01:01:25,639 --> 01:01:29,842
If you had some great trouble , Dorian , I would want to share it .

796
01:01:30,477 --> 01:01:33,554
If I were to marry you , it would be an incredible wickedness .

797
01:01:35,107 --> 01:01:38,225
Is that a way of saying you don 't love me ?

798
01:01:42,781 --> 01:01:44,398
If you like .

799
01:02:04,887 --> 01:02:08,005
It 's very beautiful , Dorian . Thank you .

800
01:02:10,934 --> 01:02:12,760
Would you find David for me ?

801
01:02:14,646 --> 01:02:16,555
I must go now .

802
01:02:38,837 --> 01:02:40,531
I 've been exploring your house , Dorian .

803
01:02:40,631 --> 01:02:42,741
You don 't mind , do you ? It 's better than a museum .

804
01:02:42,841 --> 01:02:43,909
I see .

805
01:02:44,009 --> 01:02:47,371
You must have some priceless possessions in that room if you keep them locked up .

806
01:02:47,471 --> 01:02:49,338
May I see them sometime ?

807
01:02:49,932 --> 01:02:52,126
What rare things have you stored away there , Dorian ?

808
01:02:52,226 --> 01:02:54,593
Skeletons of inquisitive guests .

809
01:02:55,229 --> 01:02:59,049
- I suspected as much . - I want to leave now , David .

810
01:02:59,149 --> 01:03:02,219
- Of course . - Good night , Dorian .

811
01:03:02,319 --> 01:03:04,346
- Good night . - Good night .

812
01:03:04,446 --> 01:03:06,021
Good night .

813
01:03:30,013 --> 01:03:33,000
It was the ninth of November , the eve of his own 38th birthday ...

814
01:03:33,100 --> 01:03:35,752
as Dorian often remembered afterwards .

815
01:03:35,852 --> 01:03:38,547
He was walking home about 11 : 00 from Lord Henry 's ...

816
01:03:38,647 --> 01:03:40,757
where he had been dining .

817
01:03:40,857 --> 01:03:43,177
A strange sense of fear for which he could not account ...

818
01:03:43,277 --> 01:03:46,054
came over him at the sight of Basil Hallward ...

819
01:03:46,154 --> 01:03:49,850
and prevented him from making any sign of recognition .

820
01:03:49,950 --> 01:03:51,400
Dorian .

821
01:03:52,661 --> 01:03:56,398
I thought it was you or your fur coat , but I wasn 't sure .

822
01:03:56,498 --> 01:03:58,066
- Didn 't you recognize me ? - In this fog ?

823
01:03:58,166 --> 01:03:59,860
I can 't even recognize Grosvenor Square .

824
01:03:59,960 --> 01:04:02,571
My house is somewhere about here , but I 'm not certain of it .

825
01:04:02,671 --> 01:04:05,115
I 've been waiting for you in your library ever since 9 : 00 .

826
01:04:05,215 --> 01:04:07,743
Finally , I took pity on your man and told him to go to bed .

827
01:04:07,843 --> 01:04:11,580
I 'm off to Paris on the midnight train , and I wanted to see you before I left .

828
01:04:11,680 --> 01:04:13,248
It 's luck running into you like this .

829
01:04:13,348 --> 01:04:16,043
I haven 't seen you in ages . I suppose you 'll be back soon .

830
01:04:16,143 --> 01:04:18,128
No . I shall be out of England for several months .

831
01:04:18,228 --> 01:04:20,756
I 'm going to take a studio in Paris and shut myself up ...

832
01:04:20,856 --> 01:04:22,883
until I finish a picture I have in my head .

833
01:04:22,983 --> 01:04:26,637
Gladys is coming over to join me later on . May I come in for a moment ?

834
01:04:26,737 --> 01:04:28,222
Won 't you miss your train ?

835
01:04:28,322 --> 01:04:31,516
It doesn 't leave until 12 : 15 , and it 's only just 11 .

836
01:04:31,616 --> 01:04:35,771
I was on my way to the club to look for you . There won 't be any delay about my luggage ...

837
01:04:35,871 --> 01:04:39,441
as I 've sent on my heavy things . All I have with me is in this bag .

838
01:04:39,541 --> 01:04:41,610
Come in , or the fog will get into the house .

839
01:04:45,213 --> 01:04:47,824
I hope you 're not going to talk about anything serious .

840
01:04:47,924 --> 01:04:51,411
Nothing is serious nowadays . At least nothing should be .

841
01:04:51,511 --> 01:04:54,331
What I have to say to you is serious , Dorian .

842
01:04:54,431 --> 01:04:58,425
Don 't frown like that . You make it so much more difficult for me .

843
01:05:00,228 --> 01:05:02,721
I hope it 's not about myself .

844
01:05:03,273 --> 01:05:04,883
I 'm tired of myself .

845
01:05:04,983 --> 01:05:08,644
It is about yourself and I must say it to you .

846
01:05:09,237 --> 01:05:12,474
- I 'll only keep you half an hour . - You sound terrifying , Basil .

847
01:05:12,574 --> 01:05:14,893
It 's for your sake I 'm speaking .

848
01:05:14,993 --> 01:05:18,445
I think you should know the things that are being said against you in London .

849
01:05:20,082 --> 01:05:23,235
I don 't want to know them . I love scandals about other people ...

850
01:05:23,335 --> 01:05:27,580
but scandals about myself don 't interest me . They lack novelty .

851
01:05:28,632 --> 01:05:31,625
You must be interested in your own reputation .

852
01:05:32,719 --> 01:05:37,165
Mind you , I don 't believe these rumors . I can 't believe them when I see you .

853
01:05:37,265 --> 01:05:39,042
There aren 't any secret vices .

854
01:05:39,142 --> 01:05:42,129
Such things write themselves across a man 's face .

855
01:05:42,229 --> 01:05:43,880
You , with your untroubled youth ...

856
01:05:43,980 --> 01:05:46,967
I find it hard to credit anything against you .

857
01:05:47,067 --> 01:05:49,845
When I hear all these hideous things that people whisper about you ...

858
01:05:49,945 --> 01:05:51,096
I don 't know what to say .

859
01:05:51,196 --> 01:05:54,266
I absolve you from the necessity of defending me .

860
01:05:54,366 --> 01:05:56,393
You can 't dismiss these charges so lightly .

861
01:05:56,493 --> 01:05:59,855
Why does a man like the Duke of Harwick leave the room of a club when you enter it ?

862
01:05:59,955 --> 01:06:03,525
Not because he knows anything about my life , but because I know everything about his .

863
01:06:03,625 --> 01:06:05,944
But why are your friendships so fatal to people ?

864
01:06:06,044 --> 01:06:08,739
There was that wretched boy in the Guards who committed suicide .

865
01:06:08,839 --> 01:06:11,658
What about Adrian Singleton and Lord Wayne 's son ?

866
01:06:11,758 --> 01:06:13,702
What gentleman will be seen with either of them ?

867
01:06:13,802 --> 01:06:16,038
The boy in the Guards was so in love with a woman ...

868
01:06:16,138 --> 01:06:18,749
he felt he couldn 't live without her . Am I to blame for that ?

869
01:06:18,849 --> 01:06:22,336
Wayne 's silly son marries a woman no one will receive . Is that my fault ?

870
01:06:22,436 --> 01:06:25,088
Adrian Singleton writes his friend 's name across a bill .

871
01:06:25,188 --> 01:06:26,715
Am I his keeper ?

872
01:06:26,815 --> 01:06:30,510
Still , one has a right to judge a man by the effect he has on his friends .

873
01:06:30,610 --> 01:06:34,063
Yours seem filled with an insatiable madness for pleasure .

874
01:06:34,698 --> 01:06:37,566
And when I think of how fond Gladys is of you .

875
01:06:38,702 --> 01:06:42,147
- What has Gladys to do with this ? - Nothing , I hope .

876
01:06:42,247 --> 01:06:44,865
And nothing in the future , if I can prevent it .

877
01:06:46,501 --> 01:06:49,279
I 'm told things it seems impossible to doubt .

878
01:06:49,379 --> 01:06:51,907
Lord Wallace was one of my greatest friends at Oxford .

879
01:06:52,007 --> 01:06:56,244
He showed me a letter that his wife had written when she was dying in her villa at Montone .

880
01:06:56,344 --> 01:06:59,915
Your name was implicated in the most terrible confession I ever read .

881
01:07:00,015 --> 01:07:02,125
I told him it was absurd ...

882
01:07:02,225 --> 01:07:06,088
that I knew you , and that you were incapable of anything of the kind .

883
01:07:06,188 --> 01:07:09,174
" Know . " Do I know you ?

884
01:07:09,274 --> 01:07:12,059
Before I could answer that , I should have to see your soul .

885
01:07:15,030 --> 01:07:17,891
- To see my soul ? - Yes . To see your soul .

886
01:07:17,991 --> 01:07:20,025
But only God can do that .

887
01:07:29,920 --> 01:07:32,705
You shall see it yourself , tonight .

888
01:07:34,466 --> 01:07:38,419
Why shouldn 't you look at it ? It 's your own handiwork .

889
01:07:38,803 --> 01:07:40,997
You can tell the world afterward if you like .

890
01:07:41,097 --> 01:07:44,376
No one will believe you . You 've chatted enough about corruption .

891
01:07:44,476 --> 01:07:46,677
Now you 'll look at it .

892
01:07:47,103 --> 01:07:49,131
I 'll show you my soul .

893
01:07:49,231 --> 01:07:52,008
I can make no sense out of what you 're saying , Dorian .

894
01:07:52,108 --> 01:07:56,972
I only ask you to give me some answer to the charges that are made against you .

895
01:07:57,072 --> 01:07:59,766
Tell me they aren 't true , and I 'll believe you .

896
01:07:59,866 --> 01:08:03,145
Come upstairs , Basil . I keep a diary of my life from day to day .

897
01:08:03,245 --> 01:08:05,188
It never leaves the room in which it is written .

898
01:08:05,288 --> 01:08:06,731
I 'll show it to you .

899
01:08:06,831 --> 01:08:10,235
I don 't want to read anything . All I want is a plain answer to my question .

900
01:08:10,335 --> 01:08:13,787
You 'll find that upstairs . You won 't have to read long .

901
01:08:49,124 --> 01:08:53,160
You 're the one man in the world who 's entitled to know everything about me .

902
01:08:55,046 --> 01:08:58,248
You 've had more to do with my life than you think .

903
01:09:07,350 --> 01:09:10,469
You think it 's only God who sees the soul .

904
01:09:46,765 --> 01:09:50,001
In spite of the indescribable corruption of the portrait ...

905
01:09:50,101 --> 01:09:54,054
Basil was still able to recognize his painting of Dorian .

906
01:10:01,696 --> 01:10:06,525
It was from within apparently that the foulness and horror came .

907
01:10:08,953 --> 01:10:14,366
It was as if some moral leprosy were eating the thing away .

908
01:10:21,508 --> 01:10:23,702
He could not believe that he had made this portrait ...

909
01:10:23,802 --> 01:10:27,546
yet there was his own name , just as he had painted it .

910
01:10:50,120 --> 01:10:54,107
But this is monstrous . It 's beyond nature , beyond reason .

911
01:10:54,207 --> 01:10:56,985
What does it mean ?

912
01:10:57,085 --> 01:11:00,196
On the day you finished this painting , I made a wish .

913
01:11:00,296 --> 01:11:02,456
Perhaps you would call it a prayer .

914
01:11:05,385 --> 01:11:07,495
My wish was granted .

915
01:11:07,595 --> 01:11:10,206
But you told me you had destroyed my painting .

916
01:11:10,306 --> 01:11:15,636
- I was wrong . It has destroyed me . - It has the eyes of a devil .

917
01:11:16,396 --> 01:11:19,341
Each of us has heaven and hell in him .

918
01:11:19,441 --> 01:11:22,218
But if this is true , if this is what you have done with your life ...

919
01:11:22,318 --> 01:11:26,021
it is far worse than anything that 's been said of you .

920
01:11:30,994 --> 01:11:33,528
Do you know how to pray , Dorian ?

921
01:11:41,171 --> 01:11:43,490
What is it we were taught to say in our boyhood ?

922
01:11:43,590 --> 01:11:46,284
Lead us not into temptation . Forgive us our sins .

923
01:11:46,384 --> 01:11:50,003
Wash away our iniquities . Let us say them together .

924
01:11:50,388 --> 01:11:53,583
- It 's too late , Basil . - The prayer of your pride was answered .

925
01:11:53,683 --> 01:11:55,842
The prayer of your repentance may be answered also .

926
01:11:59,022 --> 01:12:03,385
Do you think I haven 't tried ? I tell you , it 's no use .

927
01:12:03,485 --> 01:12:05,261
Isn 't there a verse somewhere ?

928
01:12:05,361 --> 01:12:09,398
Though your sins be as scarlet , yet I will make them white as snow .

929
01:12:13,745 --> 01:12:17,941
Only last week , Gladys recalled the day this painting was finished .

930
01:12:18,041 --> 01:12:21,319
She remembered putting her initial under my signature .

931
01:12:21,419 --> 01:12:24,079
There it is , just as she made it .

932
01:12:25,006 --> 01:12:27,249
If she could see it now .

933
01:12:30,595 --> 01:12:33,005
I can still pray , Dorian , if you can 't .

934
01:12:35,600 --> 01:12:37,919
Gladys must never know .

935
01:12:38,019 --> 01:12:42,173
Yet sometime , somehow , Basil might reveal his secret to her .

936
01:12:42,273 --> 01:12:46,518
The one person in the world whose good opinion was indispensable to him .

937
01:12:50,824 --> 01:12:54,102
An uncontrollable feeling of hatred for Basil came over him ...

938
01:12:54,202 --> 01:12:56,730
together with a terror of the knowledge he had given him ...

939
01:12:56,830 --> 01:12:58,273
and the use he might make of it .

940
01:12:58,373 --> 01:13:03,118
Panic seized him . He felt like a hunted animal , cornered , desperate .

941
01:14:21,831 --> 01:14:25,867
It was as if the painting had sweated a dew of blood .

942
01:14:48,983 --> 01:14:54,271
He felt that he had struck a mortal blow , not only at his friend but at himself .

943
01:14:55,031 --> 01:14:57,267
It seemed to him unbearable ...

944
01:14:57,367 --> 01:15:01,361
that what he had done could never be undone .

945
01:15:20,556 --> 01:15:22,465
Basil was dead .

946
01:15:23,226 --> 01:15:26,796
Men were strangled in England for what he had done .

947
01:15:26,896 --> 01:15:29,556
And yet what evidence was there against him ?

948
01:15:30,441 --> 01:15:34,888
Basil had left the house at 11 . No one had seen him come in again .

949
01:15:34,988 --> 01:15:38,773
Most of the servants were at Selby . His valet had gone to bed .

950
01:15:39,325 --> 01:15:40,476
Paris .

951
01:15:40,576 --> 01:15:45,530
It was to Paris that Basil had gone by the midnight train as he had intended .

952
01:16:31,753 --> 01:16:34,280
I 'm sorry to wake you , Francis . I forgot my latchkey .

953
01:16:34,380 --> 01:16:35,448
What time is it ?

954
01:16:35,548 --> 01:16:38,201
- Half past 12 , sir . - Half past 12 .

955
01:16:38,301 --> 01:16:40,828
You must wake me at 9 in the morning . I have some work to do .

956
01:16:40,928 --> 01:16:42,212
Yes , sir .

957
01:16:44,974 --> 01:16:46,876
Did anyone call this evening ?

958
01:16:46,976 --> 01:16:51,339
Mr. Hallward , sir . He stayed till 11 and then he went to catch his train .

959
01:16:51,439 --> 01:16:52,882
He said he was leaving for Paris .

960
01:16:52,982 --> 01:16:55,259
I 'm sorry I didn 't see him . Did he leave any message ?

961
01:16:55,359 --> 01:16:59,097
He said he would write you from Paris if he didn 't find you at your club .

962
01:16:59,197 --> 01:17:02,767
- Thank you , Francis . - Is there anything more , sir ?

963
01:17:02,867 --> 01:17:05,979
I 'm going to write a letter . I 'd like you to deliver it early in the morning .

964
01:17:06,079 --> 01:17:08,564
Mr. Allen Campbell . You 'll find the address on the envelope .

965
01:17:08,664 --> 01:17:10,949
Yes , sir . Good night , sir .

966
01:17:16,464 --> 01:17:19,993
In the morning , when Allen Campbell received his letter , he would come .

967
01:17:20,093 --> 01:17:21,918
He would come at once .

968
01:17:25,098 --> 01:17:29,585
Allen would help him . He was the only one who could help him now .

969
01:17:29,685 --> 01:17:32,755
But what if Allen Campbell should be out of England ?

970
01:17:32,855 --> 01:17:35,974
Days would pass before he could come back .

971
01:17:37,693 --> 01:17:40,312
Perhaps he would refuse to come .

972
01:17:44,075 --> 01:17:46,359
Mr. Allen Campbell , sir .

973
01:17:47,995 --> 01:17:50,189
This is kind of you , Allen .

974
01:17:56,295 --> 01:17:59,115
You said it was a matter of life and death .

975
01:17:59,215 --> 01:18:00,874
Listen to this .

976
01:18:02,718 --> 01:18:05,580
I sent my Soul through the Invisible

977
01:18:05,680 --> 01:18:08,541
Some letter of that After-life to spell :

978
01:18:08,641 --> 01:18:11,002
And by and by my Soul return 'd to me

979
01:18:11,102 --> 01:18:16,973
And answer 'd " I Myself am Heav 'n and Hell : "

980
01:18:19,694 --> 01:18:21,220
That 's quite good , don 't you think ?

981
01:18:21,320 --> 01:18:24,474
I didn 't come here to discuss the verses of Omar Khayyam .

982
01:18:24,574 --> 01:18:27,984
No , of course not . Please sit down , Allen . I 'll tell you why I sent for you .

983
01:18:32,748 --> 01:18:34,817
Allen , in a locked room at the top of this house ...

984
01:18:34,917 --> 01:18:37,904
a room to which no one but myself has access ...

985
01:18:38,004 --> 01:18:40,782
a dead man is lying across a table .

986
01:18:40,882 --> 01:18:43,117
He 's been dead for 10 hours .

987
01:18:43,217 --> 01:18:46,996
Who he is , why he died , how he died , are matters that do not concern you .

988
01:18:47,096 --> 01:18:49,415
- What you must do is ... - There 's no need for you to go on .

989
01:18:49,515 --> 01:18:51,383
Your horrible secrets don 't interest me .

990
01:18:56,105 --> 01:18:58,716
They 'll have to interest you .

991
01:18:58,816 --> 01:19:01,469
You are the one man who is able to save me .

992
01:19:01,569 --> 01:19:02,845
You are scientific , Allen .

993
01:19:02,945 --> 01:19:06,432
I have seen your name in scientific reviews in connection with certain experiments .

994
01:19:06,532 --> 01:19:08,101
What has that to do with you ?

995
01:19:08,201 --> 01:19:11,312
What you have got to do is to destroy the thing that is upstairs .

996
01:19:11,412 --> 01:19:13,689
Destroy it so that not a vestige is left .

997
01:19:13,789 --> 01:19:17,652
Nobody saw this person come into the house . He is supposed to be in Paris .

998
01:19:17,752 --> 01:19:20,822
When he is missed , not a trace of him must be found here .

999
01:19:20,922 --> 01:19:23,616
You must change him and everything that belongs to him ...

1000
01:19:23,716 --> 01:19:27,036
including his coat and his traveling bag , which I have locked up in this room ...

1001
01:19:27,136 --> 01:19:28,496
into a handful of ashes .

1002
01:19:28,596 --> 01:19:32,966
You must be insane to suppose I 'd lift a finger to help you .

1003
01:19:33,643 --> 01:19:37,046
- It was suicide , Allen . - What drove him to it ?

1004
01:19:37,146 --> 01:19:38,631
You won 't do this for me ?

1005
01:19:38,731 --> 01:19:42,308
How can you ask me , of all men , to mix myself up in this horror ?

1006
01:19:44,487 --> 01:19:48,898
Allen , it was murder . I killed him .

1007
01:19:50,618 --> 01:19:52,562
He was responsible for the ruin of my life .

1008
01:19:52,662 --> 01:19:54,856
He didn 't intend it , but the result was the same .

1009
01:19:54,956 --> 01:19:56,315
You are certain to be caught .

1010
01:19:56,415 --> 01:19:59,861
No man commits a crime without doing something stupid .

1011
01:19:59,961 --> 01:20:03,239
- I 'll have no part of it . - We were friends once , Allen .

1012
01:20:03,339 --> 01:20:04,699
I regret that .

1013
01:20:04,799 --> 01:20:07,577
Don 't you understand that if you don 't help me , I 'm lost ?

1014
01:20:07,677 --> 01:20:10,955
- They will hang me for what I have done . - Let them .

1015
01:20:11,055 --> 01:20:13,666
- You refuse ? - Yes .

1016
01:20:13,766 --> 01:20:15,758
- I entreat you . - It 's useless .

1017
01:20:17,645 --> 01:20:20,798
I 'm sorry , Allen . You leave me no alternative .

1018
01:20:20,898 --> 01:20:24,184
I 've written a letter . Here it is .

1019
01:20:26,028 --> 01:20:28,014
You see the address .

1020
01:20:28,114 --> 01:20:31,934
If you don 't help me , I must send it . If you don 't help me , I will send it .

1021
01:20:32,034 --> 01:20:34,819
You know what the result will be .

1022
01:20:44,505 --> 01:20:46,331
The thing is quite simple , Allen .

1023
01:20:47,675 --> 01:20:49,667
It would kill her .

1024
01:20:50,386 --> 01:20:54,130
I didn 't think you would want her name involved in such a scandal .

1025
01:20:56,767 --> 01:20:58,794
I cannot do it .

1026
01:20:58,894 --> 01:21:00,470
You have no choice .

1027
01:21:05,693 --> 01:21:10,688
I shall have to go home and get some things from the laboratory .

1028
01:21:15,161 --> 01:21:17,403
You 've saved my life .

1029
01:21:27,590 --> 01:21:30,159
Dorian dined that evening with Lady Narborough ...

1030
01:21:30,259 --> 01:21:32,954
who had what Lord Henry described as ...

1031
01:21:33,054 --> 01:21:36,589
the remains of a really remarkable ugliness .

1032
01:21:37,975 --> 01:21:39,418
You left early last night , Dorian .

1033
01:21:39,518 --> 01:21:42,129
Did you go straight home , or did you go to the club ?

1034
01:21:42,229 --> 01:21:45,591
Why are you so inquisitive , Harry ? I came in at half past 12 .

1035
01:21:45,691 --> 01:21:48,052
If you want any corroborative evidence , you can ask my man .

1036
01:21:48,152 --> 01:21:51,347
- Remember your promise , Lord Henry . - There are two hours unaccounted for ...

1037
01:21:51,447 --> 01:21:54,392
I suspect will bear investigation . Or perhaps they will not .

1038
01:21:54,492 --> 01:21:56,686
You 've hardly touched my beautiful dinner , Lord Henry .

1039
01:21:56,786 --> 01:21:57,895
I believe you 're in love .

1040
01:21:57,995 --> 01:22:00,481
I haven 't been in love . Not since Madame de Farrol left .

1041
01:22:00,581 --> 01:22:02,733
- Madame de Farrol ? - She 's a wonderful woman .

1042
01:22:02,833 --> 01:22:05,569
When her third husband died , her hair turned quite gold from grief .

1043
01:22:05,669 --> 01:22:07,196
What 's her fourth husband like ?

1044
01:22:07,296 --> 01:22:09,699
Husbands of beautiful women belong to the criminal classes .

1045
01:22:09,799 --> 01:22:12,159
I 'm not surprised that the world says you 're wicked .

1046
01:22:12,259 --> 01:22:15,162
What world says that , Lady Narborough ? It can only be the next world .

1047
01:22:15,262 --> 01:22:17,206
This world and Harry are on excellent terms .

1048
01:22:17,306 --> 01:22:18,874
Everyone I know says he 's wicked .

1049
01:22:18,974 --> 01:22:21,043
It 's monstrous the way people go about nowadays ...

1050
01:22:21,143 --> 01:22:25,214
saying things behind one 's back that are absolutely and entirely true .

1051
01:22:25,314 --> 01:22:26,966
Women love us for our defects .

1052
01:22:27,066 --> 01:22:30,511
If we have enough of them , they 'll forgive us anything , even our intellects .

1053
01:22:30,611 --> 01:22:33,514
At any rate , no one 'll ever persuade me that Mr. Gray is wicked .

1054
01:22:33,614 --> 01:22:36,225
And I shall never forgive him for remaining a bachelor .

1055
01:22:36,325 --> 01:22:38,686
Don 't you think we ought to find a wife for Mr. Gray ?

1056
01:22:38,786 --> 01:22:40,104
I 'm always telling him so .

1057
01:22:40,204 --> 01:22:42,189
I shall go through Debrett tonight ...

1058
01:22:42,289 --> 01:22:44,900
and draw out a list of all the eligible young ladies .

1059
01:22:45,000 --> 01:22:47,862
- With their ages ? - Only slightly edited .

1060
01:22:47,962 --> 01:22:51,324
I want it to be a suitable alliance . I want you both to be happy .

1061
01:22:51,424 --> 01:22:53,492
I shall save you the trouble of looking .

1062
01:22:53,592 --> 01:22:56,037
I have already chosen her , if she will have me .

1063
01:22:56,137 --> 01:22:58,414
I don 't believe it .

1064
01:22:58,514 --> 01:23:01,007
Gladys , darling . Will you marry me ?

1065
01:23:10,192 --> 01:23:12,303
Of course I will , darling .

1066
01:23:12,403 --> 01:23:14,597
This is the only marriage I 've ever approved of .

1067
01:23:14,697 --> 01:23:16,599
- How exciting . - That is a stunner .

1068
01:23:16,699 --> 01:23:19,060
- I 'm so happy for you . - I congratulate you both .

1069
01:23:26,083 --> 01:23:29,111
For months , the mysterious disappearance of Basil Hallward ...

1070
01:23:29,211 --> 01:23:31,454
was the sensation of London .

1071
01:23:34,884 --> 01:23:37,119
You don 't mind if I go on with my work while we talk ?

1072
01:23:37,219 --> 01:23:39,830
- Not at all . - It 's a matter of some urgency .

1073
01:23:39,930 --> 01:23:43,292
- Tell me what you discovered in France . - We discovered nothing , nothing at all .

1074
01:23:43,392 --> 01:23:46,128
We hunted up everyone even remotely acquainted with my uncle ...

1075
01:23:46,228 --> 01:23:48,130
but not one had seen him or heard from him .

1076
01:23:48,230 --> 01:23:50,633
The Paris police don 't believe he ever arrived in France .

1077
01:23:50,733 --> 01:23:54,095
And here , at Scotland Yard , we 're equally convinced he did leave London .

1078
01:23:54,195 --> 01:23:57,056
The man in the gray ulster who boarded the train at Victoria Station ...

1079
01:23:57,156 --> 01:23:58,731
was undoubtedly Basil Hallward .

1080
01:24:00,868 --> 01:24:02,895
What are we to do now ?

1081
01:24:02,995 --> 01:24:06,899
You 're both young . I understand you 're engaged to marry .

1082
01:24:06,999 --> 01:24:11,237
Go on with your own lives peacefully . Believe me , that 's the best course .

1083
01:24:11,337 --> 01:24:13,781
I promise you , Scotland Yard will not forget Basil Hallward .

1084
01:24:13,881 --> 01:24:16,659
I thought it might be good for Gladys to go away for a while .

1085
01:24:16,759 --> 01:24:17,827
It would be .

1086
01:24:17,927 --> 01:24:19,662
I 'm going to Selby tomorrow .

1087
01:24:19,762 --> 01:24:22,373
I 've persuaded Gladys to join me with some friends on Thursday .

1088
01:24:22,473 --> 01:24:25,709
Others are coming for the pheasant shooting . We 'd be delighted if you 'd join us .

1089
01:24:25,809 --> 01:24:28,170
Oh , I 'm afraid I can 't get away . But I 'm glad you 're going .

1090
01:24:28,270 --> 01:24:29,797
The diversion will do you good .

1091
01:24:29,897 --> 01:24:31,799
Thank you , Sir Robert . You 've been very kind .

1092
01:24:31,899 --> 01:24:33,349
Not at all .

1093
01:24:36,487 --> 01:24:38,180
Mr. Gray ?

1094
01:24:38,280 --> 01:24:41,023
Are you acquainted with a young man named Allen Campbell ?

1095
01:24:42,326 --> 01:24:44,353
Why , yes . At one time we were great friends .

1096
01:24:44,453 --> 01:24:47,773
It 's been a long time since I 've seen him . Why do you ask ?

1097
01:24:47,873 --> 01:24:50,818
I 've just received a very tragic notice .

1098
01:24:50,918 --> 01:24:54,287
This morning , Allen Campbell died by his own hand .

1099
01:24:54,838 --> 01:24:57,867
- Why on earth should Allen Campbell ? - Why , indeed .

1100
01:24:57,967 --> 01:25:00,870
I thought you might give me a clue . He had everything to live for .

1101
01:25:00,970 --> 01:25:03,998
He was just beginning to achieve a name for himself in science .

1102
01:25:04,098 --> 01:25:07,376
He left no note or letter , no explanation of any sort ?

1103
01:25:07,476 --> 01:25:11,213
None . Whatever drove him to it , he took the secret with him .

1104
01:25:11,313 --> 01:25:14,640
How little we really know of what goes on inside a man .

1105
01:25:17,653 --> 01:25:19,145
Yes .

1106
01:25:23,742 --> 01:25:27,236
You 've been sad all evening . Is it Allen Campbell ?

1107
01:25:27,788 --> 01:25:30,364
- Perhaps . - I 'm sorry .

1108
01:25:37,631 --> 01:25:39,533
Let 's be married soon , in a fortnight .

1109
01:25:39,633 --> 01:25:42,495
A simple wedding with only our closest friends .

1110
01:25:42,595 --> 01:25:44,962
A fortnight ? You call that soon ?

1111
01:25:56,859 --> 01:25:58,093
Good night , darling .

1112
01:25:58,193 --> 01:26:00,554
I 'll come to Selby on Thursday afternoon with Janet .

1113
01:26:00,654 --> 01:26:02,730
I 'll be at the station .

1114
01:26:12,166 --> 01:26:14,568
Allen Campbell .

1115
01:26:14,668 --> 01:26:18,037
Would Allen 's blood be on the painting now ?

1116
01:26:18,672 --> 01:26:23,827
There were other roads to forgetfulness than the one that Allen took .

1117
01:26:23,927 --> 01:26:26,379
- Where to , sir ? - Bluegate Fields .

1118
01:26:28,557 --> 01:26:30,299
Yes , sir .

1119
01:26:31,769 --> 01:26:35,631
One day we shall be awakened with suffering and dismay ...

1120
01:26:35,731 --> 01:26:39,593
to the realization that the soul is not a superstition .

1121
01:26:39,693 --> 01:26:45,731
Nor the spirit of man , a material substance that can be viewed under a microscope .

1122
01:26:46,492 --> 01:26:50,570
The eternal words are as true today as when he uttered them .

1123
01:26:51,205 --> 01:26:55,401
What shall it profit a man if he gain the whole world ...

1124
01:26:55,501 --> 01:26:57,987
and lose his soul ?

1125
01:26:58,087 --> 01:27:00,447
The soul is not an illusion .

1126
01:27:00,547 --> 01:27:03,033
It is a terrible reality .

1127
01:27:03,133 --> 01:27:06,412
It can be bought and sold and bartered away .

1128
01:27:06,512 --> 01:27:09,255
It can be poisoned or made perfect .

1129
01:27:10,057 --> 01:27:15,504
That man , rich or poor , who has the light of faith and charity within himself ...

1130
01:27:15,604 --> 01:27:19,056
even though he were plunged into the very pit of darkness ...

1131
01:27:19,608 --> 01:27:23,436
would still enjoy the clear light of day .

1132
01:27:24,405 --> 01:27:28,350
But the wretched creature whose soul is filled with dark thoughts ...

1133
01:27:28,450 --> 01:27:31,604
and foul deeds must dwell in darkness .

1134
01:27:31,704 --> 01:27:34,982
Even though he walk under the noonday sun ...

1135
01:27:35,082 --> 01:27:38,492
he must carry his own vile dungeon round with him .

1136
01:28:55,954 --> 01:28:58,322
What 's that you 're playing ?

1137
01:28:59,041 --> 01:29:00,866
It has a name , hasn 't it ?

1138
01:29:02,211 --> 01:29:04,947
A kind of name .

1139
01:29:05,047 --> 01:29:08,040
It 's called " Prelude . "

1140
01:29:09,176 --> 01:29:10,876
Play something else .

1141
01:29:24,149 --> 01:29:26,802
Why you do not like that music ?

1142
01:29:26,902 --> 01:29:30,187
I heard someone play that piece before .

1143
01:29:34,576 --> 01:29:37,570
- Eighteen years ago . - A woman ?

1144
01:29:40,165 --> 01:29:43,576
Every time I get back to London , I look for him .

1145
01:29:44,086 --> 01:29:48,372
" Sir Tristan , " my sister called him . Because he was like a knight .

1146
01:29:49,424 --> 01:29:53,162
If he was in Rangoon or Valparaiso , I 'd find him .

1147
01:29:53,262 --> 01:29:57,089
But in London , it 's like looking for a needle in a haystack .

1148
01:29:58,058 --> 01:30:00,259
I don 't know his real name .

1149
01:30:01,395 --> 01:30:03,589
I don 't even know what he looks like .

1150
01:30:03,689 --> 01:30:05,765
And when you find him , what will you do ?

1151
01:30:11,572 --> 01:30:15,024
Maybe he 's dead already . Did you think of that ?

1152
01:30:23,750 --> 01:30:25,868
I 'll keep on looking .

1153
01:30:29,214 --> 01:30:31,415
You 're not English .

1154
01:30:31,967 --> 01:30:34,085
What is English ?

1155
01:30:34,678 --> 01:30:38,964
There are men and there are women .

1156
01:30:41,685 --> 01:30:44,379
This is Sir Tristan , Kate darling .

1157
01:30:44,479 --> 01:30:46,632
I 've asked you not to call me that , Adrian .

1158
01:30:46,732 --> 01:30:50,976
I heard Lord Henry call you Sir Tristan , and at the time I thought it fit .

1159
01:30:52,321 --> 01:30:56,315
- Why do we never see you ? - I have all I need here .

1160
01:30:57,159 --> 01:31:01,112
Drink and drugs and no friends .

1161
01:31:02,289 --> 01:31:04,615
I 've had too many friends .

1162
01:31:06,043 --> 01:31:10,246
Oh , he 's drawing a picture of you , sir . Come and look at it .

1163
01:31:10,881 --> 01:31:15,876
What would you like ? A song , a poem , a painting ?

1164
01:31:18,513 --> 01:31:21,340
I do all three surpassingly well .

1165
01:31:24,770 --> 01:31:27,513
It seems to me there 's something lacking .

1166
01:31:34,863 --> 01:31:36,355
I have it .

1167
01:31:38,617 --> 01:31:41,110
But grim to see

1168
01:31:46,333 --> 01:31:48,409
Is the gallows-tree

1169
01:31:49,211 --> 01:31:51,162
Goodbye , Adrian .

1170
01:31:53,048 --> 01:31:57,786
And , green or dry , a man must die Before it bears its fruit !

1171
01:31:57,886 --> 01:31:59,461
Goodbye , Sir Tristan .

1172
01:32:07,437 --> 01:32:09,221
What did you call him ?

1173
01:32:11,483 --> 01:32:13,010
Sit down .

1174
01:32:13,110 --> 01:32:16,437
I 'll draw your picture for the price of three drinks .

1175
01:32:17,280 --> 01:32:20,058
- Four drinks . - Sir Tristan , you said .

1176
01:32:20,158 --> 01:32:24,945
And Sir Tristan rode forth into the forest , seeking his only love .

1177
01:32:26,665 --> 01:32:28,782
He has gone to kill your friend .

1178
01:32:30,836 --> 01:32:33,579
Justice has come to England ...

1179
01:32:35,007 --> 01:32:37,625
without wig or gown .

1180
01:32:38,093 --> 01:32:39,919
Come on , Kate .

1181
01:32:42,556 --> 01:32:44,917
- If it 's money you want ... - I 'm Sibyl Vane 's brother .

1182
01:32:45,017 --> 01:32:47,169
- Does that mean anything to you ? - No , nothing .

1183
01:32:47,269 --> 01:32:49,504
Why are you called Sir Tristan ?

1184
01:32:49,604 --> 01:32:50,923
It happens to be my name .

1185
01:32:51,023 --> 01:32:54,593
You 're lying . Eighteen years I 've been looking for you .

1186
01:32:54,693 --> 01:32:56,810
How old do you think I am ?

1187
01:33:18,717 --> 01:33:22,037
Why didn 't you murder him ? They could only have hanged you for it .

1188
01:33:22,137 --> 01:33:25,832
He 's not the man I 'm looking for . He 's too young .

1189
01:33:25,932 --> 01:33:29,176
- How old do you think he is ? - Twenty-two , I 'd say .

1190
01:33:31,104 --> 01:33:33,305
What are you laughing at ?

1191
01:33:34,149 --> 01:33:38,143
Dorian Gray has looked 22 for the last 20 years .

1192
01:33:41,490 --> 01:33:43,649
What did you say his name was ?

1193
01:34:15,065 --> 01:34:18,343
When a man says he 's exhausted life , you may be sure that life has exhausted him .

1194
01:34:18,443 --> 01:34:20,554
But in your case , this strange impulse to be good ...

1195
01:34:20,654 --> 01:34:22,514
is the effect of your approaching marriage .

1196
01:34:22,614 --> 01:34:25,434
It will wear off in time . Do you mind pulling down that blind ?

1197
01:34:25,534 --> 01:34:29,271
Not at all . The truth is I want to be better . I 'm determined to be better .

1198
01:34:29,371 --> 01:34:32,107
At least it will be a novel sensation , and needn 't become a habit .

1199
01:34:32,207 --> 01:34:36,160
Marriage itself is merely a habit , a very bad habit .

1200
01:34:36,670 --> 01:34:39,031
I trust it won 't make you a hopelessly reformed character .

1201
01:34:39,131 --> 01:34:42,200
Harry , I 've been away so long . What are people talking about in London ?

1202
01:34:42,300 --> 01:34:44,161
They were talking about Basil 's disappearance .

1203
01:34:44,261 --> 01:34:47,289
But now they are completely taken up with Allen Campbell 's suicide .

1204
01:34:47,389 --> 01:34:49,958
- What do you think happened to Basil ? - I haven 't the slightest .

1205
01:34:50,058 --> 01:34:53,295
I suppose in a fortnight , we shall be told that he 's been seen in San Francisco .

1206
01:34:53,395 --> 01:34:56,423
Everyone who disappears is said to be seen in San Francisco .

1207
01:34:56,523 --> 01:34:59,593
It must be a delightful city and possess the attractions of the next world .

1208
01:34:59,693 --> 01:35:02,137
He was a fine painter . I 'm certain of that .

1209
01:35:02,237 --> 01:35:05,098
The best thing that Basil ever did was that wonderful portrait of you .

1210
01:35:05,198 --> 01:35:07,934
I remember you told me it was stolen or destroyed or something .

1211
01:35:08,034 --> 01:35:09,102
What is your secret ?

1212
01:35:09,202 --> 01:35:12,022
You don 't look a day older than you did when that portrait was painted .

1213
01:35:12,122 --> 01:35:14,107
Perhaps I 'll tell you some day .

1214
01:35:14,207 --> 01:35:16,359
To get back my youth , I 'd do anything in the world ...

1215
01:35:16,459 --> 01:35:19,370
except get up early , take exercise or be respectable .

1216
01:35:20,130 --> 01:35:24,375
I sometimes think I 'd give anything if I could change and grow old like other people .

1217
01:35:49,534 --> 01:35:52,444
My good resolutions may have come too late .

1218
01:35:53,413 --> 01:35:56,650
Though Dorian placed guards about the estate ...

1219
01:35:56,750 --> 01:35:59,986
the consciousness of being hunted , snared , tracked down ...

1220
01:36:00,086 --> 01:36:02,531
began to dominate him .

1221
01:36:02,631 --> 01:36:04,116
In the small hours of the night ...

1222
01:36:04,216 --> 01:36:07,702
when every sound is seized upon by the distraught imagination ...

1223
01:36:07,802 --> 01:36:10,963
remorse and terror laid hold of him .

1224
01:36:11,640 --> 01:36:16,670
Each detail of his crimes came back to him in nightmares with added horror ...

1225
01:36:16,770 --> 01:36:20,973
haunting him relentlessly with the living death of his soul .

1226
01:36:24,486 --> 01:36:30,816
With the day came the cruel necessity to dissemble to Gladys and to his guests .

1227
01:36:36,957 --> 01:36:39,025
- Have you had good sport , Geoffrey ? - Not very good .

1228
01:36:39,125 --> 01:36:41,111
I think most of the birds have gone to the open .

1229
01:36:41,211 --> 01:36:43,912
It may be better after lunch , when we get to new ground .

1230
01:36:48,927 --> 01:36:51,503
- Don 't shoot it , Geoffrey . - Nonsense !

1231
01:36:54,182 --> 01:36:56,084
Good heavens , I 've hit a beater .

1232
01:36:56,184 --> 01:36:58,295
What an idiot the man was to get in front of the gun .

1233
01:36:58,395 --> 01:37:00,422
Stop shooting there . A man 's hurt .

1234
01:37:00,522 --> 01:37:02,257
Where sir ? Where is he ?

1235
01:37:02,357 --> 01:37:05,510
Here . Why on earth don 't you keep your men back ?

1236
01:37:05,610 --> 01:37:07,686
Spoiled my shooting for the day .

1237
01:37:20,875 --> 01:37:23,528
The shooting 's stopped for today . It wouldn 't look well to go on .

1238
01:37:23,628 --> 01:37:24,946
- Is the man ? - Yes , he 's dead .

1239
01:37:25,046 --> 01:37:27,414
He received a full charge in his chest .

1240
01:37:31,636 --> 01:37:32,746
Thornton , come in .

1241
01:37:32,846 --> 01:37:35,498
I suppose you 've come about the unfortunate accident this morning .

1242
01:37:35,598 --> 01:37:39,377
Was he married ? Did he have any dependents ? I 'll write them any sum you think necessary .

1243
01:37:39,477 --> 01:37:42,714
We don 't know who he is , sir . That 's why I took the liberty of coming to you .

1244
01:37:42,814 --> 01:37:45,300
- Wasn 't he one of your men ? - No , sir . Never saw him before .

1245
01:37:45,400 --> 01:37:47,351
Seems like a sailor .

1246
01:37:48,194 --> 01:37:50,972
- A sailor . - Looks as if he 'd been a sort of sailor .

1247
01:37:51,072 --> 01:37:53,808
Tattooed on both arms and that kind of thing .

1248
01:37:53,908 --> 01:37:56,561
Wasn 't anything found on him ? Anything that would tell his name ?

1249
01:37:56,661 --> 01:37:58,772
Some money , not much , and a six-shooter .

1250
01:37:58,872 --> 01:38:00,232
No name of any kind .

1251
01:38:00,332 --> 01:38:04,903
Decent-looking man , sir . But rough-like . A sort of sailor , we think .

1252
01:38:05,003 --> 01:38:08,330
- Where is the body ? - In an empty stable at the home farm , sir .

1253
01:38:18,433 --> 01:38:20,259
Show me his face .

1254
01:38:43,249 --> 01:38:44,866
Come in .

1255
01:38:46,503 --> 01:38:48,571
What is it , Dorian ?

1256
01:38:48,671 --> 01:38:51,623
Oh , but you haven 't changed . You 'll be late for dinner .

1257
01:38:54,302 --> 01:38:56,336
I wanted to look at you .

1258
01:38:58,681 --> 01:39:02,301
I know , darling . I 've felt that way so often about you .

1259
01:39:12,237 --> 01:39:16,398
- Goodbye , Gladys . - Goodbye ? Until half past 8 .

1260
01:39:19,035 --> 01:39:20,819
Until half past 8 .

1261
01:39:41,141 --> 01:39:42,299
Go on .

1262
01:39:46,354 --> 01:39:49,264
- Shall I go on , sir ? - Yes .

1263
01:39:51,359 --> 01:39:52,893
Dorian .

1264
01:39:54,070 --> 01:39:55,646
Dorian !

1265
01:40:12,630 --> 01:40:16,375
David . What brings you to Selby ? Have you seen Dorian ?

1266
01:40:17,260 --> 01:40:19,162
Well , what is it ? What 's happened ?

1267
01:40:19,262 --> 01:40:21,289
Dorian 's gone to London . Didn 't you know ?

1268
01:40:21,389 --> 01:40:23,208
David passed him on his way from the station .

1269
01:40:23,308 --> 01:40:25,794
- It 's strange , his rushing away . - He looked black as thunder .

1270
01:40:25,894 --> 01:40:27,754
I thought he 'd found out what I 've been up to .

1271
01:40:27,854 --> 01:40:29,763
What have you been up to , David ?

1272
01:40:31,232 --> 01:40:34,135
You 'll put it down to jealousy . I don 't deny jealousy 's mixed up in it .

1273
01:40:34,235 --> 01:40:35,887
I had a dreadful presentiment about you .

1274
01:40:35,987 --> 01:40:38,223
And when you announced the date of your marriage , I ...

1275
01:40:38,323 --> 01:40:40,850
I grew desperate . I wanted to do anything to try and stop it .

1276
01:40:40,950 --> 01:40:43,068
What is it you 've done , David ?

1277
01:40:43,953 --> 01:40:46,064
There is a locked room at the top of Dorian 's house .

1278
01:40:46,164 --> 01:40:47,816
I didn 't think it was important at first .

1279
01:40:47,916 --> 01:40:50,276
He could have locked up anything he wanted to keep safe ...

1280
01:40:50,376 --> 01:40:51,820
from the servants even .

1281
01:40:51,920 --> 01:40:54,989
But then one of Dorian 's valets came to see me about a position .

1282
01:40:55,089 --> 01:40:57,659
It struck me how often Dorian changed his servants .

1283
01:40:57,759 --> 01:41:01,663
This one told me that Dorian would go into that room at all hours and lock himself in .

1284
01:41:01,763 --> 01:41:05,667
One night he heard a noise and went to investigate . It was 4 : 00 in the morning .

1285
01:41:05,767 --> 01:41:08,628
Dorian came out of the room and looked at him in the strangest way .

1286
01:41:08,728 --> 01:41:10,713
As if he could kill him , he said .

1287
01:41:10,813 --> 01:41:13,466
Then he accused him of spying and sacked him .

1288
01:41:13,566 --> 01:41:15,677
I began to feel that if I could get into that room ...

1289
01:41:15,777 --> 01:41:18,763
I might find something that would put a stop to this marriage .

1290
01:41:18,863 --> 01:41:20,188
And did you get in ?

1291
01:41:27,455 --> 01:41:30,733
I bribed one of his servants to get me an impression of the lock .

1292
01:41:30,833 --> 01:41:32,659
Here 's the key .

1293
01:41:34,170 --> 01:41:38,039
I waited until Dorian came down here to Selby and then I let myself in .

1294
01:41:38,967 --> 01:41:42,370
I know you 'll despise me for stooping to such measures , but I 'm not important .

1295
01:41:42,470 --> 01:41:45,331
It doesn 't matter what happens to me or even what you think of me ...

1296
01:41:45,431 --> 01:41:48,592
- ... if I can stop you from marrying him . - What did you find in the room ?

1297
01:41:49,811 --> 01:41:52,380
Nothing to help me , really . It 's just an old schoolroom .

1298
01:41:52,480 --> 01:41:54,549
And there 's a huge portrait with a covering over it .

1299
01:41:54,649 --> 01:41:57,893
- A portrait ? Of whom ? - I don 't know .

1300
01:41:58,611 --> 01:42:01,931
The original must be a monstrous person , if an original exists .

1301
01:42:02,031 --> 01:42:06,227
It has a vague family resemblance to Dorian . A sort of middle-aged , mad , gruesome uncle ...

1302
01:42:06,327 --> 01:42:09,112
with a debauched face and blood all over him .

1303
01:42:09,872 --> 01:42:11,900
It was painted by your uncle .

1304
01:42:12,000 --> 01:42:15,494
- My uncle never painted such a picture . - He signed it .

1305
01:42:17,589 --> 01:42:19,574
I 'd been counting so much on finding something ...

1306
01:42:19,674 --> 01:42:21,910
that I decided it was just jealousy on my part ...

1307
01:42:22,010 --> 01:42:24,662
and I 'd been doing Dorian a great injustice .

1308
01:42:24,762 --> 01:42:28,500
I had an impulse to come down here and make a clean breast of it to both of you .

1309
01:42:28,600 --> 01:42:30,835
Give you my blessing and ask your forgiveness .

1310
01:42:30,935 --> 01:42:33,303
Can you describe the portrait in greater detail ?

1311
01:42:34,522 --> 01:42:37,717
There 's a curious cat in it . Like the one in Dorian 's drawing room .

1312
01:42:37,817 --> 01:42:42,437
Only in the portrait the eyes shine in an evil way that 's indescribable .

1313
01:42:49,078 --> 01:42:52,524
Did you notice anything unusual about the signature ?

1314
01:42:52,624 --> 01:42:54,324
No , I don 't think so .

1315
01:42:56,919 --> 01:42:59,280
Now that I see you , Gladys . I can 't say what I intended to .

1316
01:42:59,380 --> 01:43:00,990
I 'd be lying if I did .

1317
01:43:01,090 --> 01:43:03,535
I know this marriage is wrong . You can 't go through with it .

1318
01:43:03,635 --> 01:43:05,870
There 's something strange and evil in Dorian .

1319
01:43:05,970 --> 01:43:09,707
Was there a letter G under the signature on that painting , David ?

1320
01:43:09,807 --> 01:43:11,424
Like this ?

1321
01:43:12,727 --> 01:43:15,463
I believe there was . How did you know ?

1322
01:43:20,902 --> 01:43:23,763
- Yes , Gibson ? - I beg your pardon , miss .

1323
01:43:23,863 --> 01:43:27,267
But Mr. Gray asked me to bring you this letter when I got back from the station .

1324
01:43:27,367 --> 01:43:30,694
- He said I must give it to you in person . - Thank you .

1325
01:43:45,301 --> 01:43:47,579
Once I said that if I were to marry you ...

1326
01:43:47,679 --> 01:43:49,747
it would be an incredible wickedness .

1327
01:43:49,847 --> 01:43:52,959
You thought it was a way of saying that I didn 't love you .

1328
01:43:53,059 --> 01:43:57,130
You must know that I do love you , more than anything in the world .

1329
01:43:57,230 --> 01:44:00,258
But I can only bring disaster on those who love me .

1330
01:44:00,358 --> 01:44:05,179
If you knew how I 've already wronged you , you would turn from me in horror .

1331
01:44:05,279 --> 01:44:07,307
You will never see me again .

1332
01:44:07,407 --> 01:44:11,693
Try to remember me , dear Gladys , without bitterness .

1333
01:44:12,161 --> 01:44:16,364
This is the only good thing I have ever done .

1334
01:44:18,209 --> 01:44:21,703
Won 't you tell us what it is , Gladys ? Perhaps we can help you .

1335
01:44:25,717 --> 01:44:27,959
We must go to London at once .

1336
01:44:35,435 --> 01:44:38,511
Was it true that one could never change ?

1337
01:44:39,480 --> 01:44:42,216
He longed for the unstained purity of his youth ...

1338
01:44:42,316 --> 01:44:45,178
before he had prayed in a monstrous moment of pride and passion ...

1339
01:44:45,278 --> 01:44:49,981
that the painting should bear the burden of the years and of his corruption .

1340
01:44:52,326 --> 01:44:54,110
Sibyl Vane was dead .

1341
01:44:54,620 --> 01:44:57,732
And now her brother would be hidden in a nameless grave .

1342
01:44:57,832 --> 01:44:59,984
Allen Campbell had shot himself .

1343
01:45:00,084 --> 01:45:01,576
And Basil ...

1344
01:45:07,175 --> 01:45:09,209
Nothing could alter that .

1345
01:45:10,720 --> 01:45:13,672
It was of the future that he must think .

1346
01:45:15,516 --> 01:45:17,669
He had spared Gladys .

1347
01:45:17,769 --> 01:45:21,346
Would there be any sign of his one good deed in the portrait ?

1348
01:45:44,170 --> 01:45:50,159
It was there , almost imperceptible , but surely it was there in the eyes ...

1349
01:45:50,259 --> 01:45:53,287
struggling through the horror and the loathsomeness .

1350
01:45:53,387 --> 01:45:55,839
There was hope for him , then .

1351
01:45:58,601 --> 01:46:02,130
He would go away , leave England forever , live obscurely in a distant country ...

1352
01:46:02,230 --> 01:46:05,717
find peace in a life of humility and self-denial .

1353
01:46:05,817 --> 01:46:09,429
He would expel every sign of evil from the painted face .

1354
01:46:09,529 --> 01:46:12,856
He would watch the hideousness fade and change .

1355
01:46:13,825 --> 01:46:17,610
But the painting would always be there to tempt his weakness .

1356
01:46:18,412 --> 01:46:20,148
Better to destroy it ...

1357
01:46:20,248 --> 01:46:22,775
to grow old inevitably as all men grow old .

1358
01:46:22,875 --> 01:46:26,904
If he fell into evil ways , to be punished as all men are punished .

1359
01:46:27,004 --> 01:46:32,500
Better if each sin of his life were to bring its sure , swift penalty .

1360
01:46:33,678 --> 01:46:37,665
The knife that had killed Basil Hallward would kill his portrait also ...

1361
01:46:37,765 --> 01:46:42,177
and free him at a stroke from the evil enchantment of the past .

1362
01:47:03,457 --> 01:47:07,028
But when the knife pierced the heart of the portrait ...

1363
01:47:07,128 --> 01:47:09,788
an extraordinary thing happened .

1364
01:47:42,538 --> 01:47:45,650
Pray , Father , forgive me . Pray , Father , forgive me for I have sinned .

1365
01:47:45,750 --> 01:47:47,652
Pray , Father , forgive me for I have sinned .

1366
01:47:47,752 --> 01:47:50,870
Through my fault , through my most grievous faults .

1367
01:48:39,053 --> 01:48:41,337
Heaven forgive me .

1368
01:48:53,693 --> 01:48:55,894
Take Gladys home , David .

